nto de software","como usar ferramentas de IA para desenvolvimento de software","o que é ferramenta de especificação de produto","ferramenta de especificação de produto vs outras ferramentas"],"ru":["инструмент для создания спецификаций продукта","разработка программных продуктов с ИИ Агентами","руководства по спецификации продукта","планирование реализации с ИИ Агентами","технические документы для ИИ Агентов","альтернативы инструментам разработки программного обеспечения","как использовать ИИ Агенты для разработки программного обеспечения","что такое инструмент для создания спецификаций продукта","инструмент для создания спецификаций продукта vs другие инструменты"],"ar":["أداة مواصفات المنتج","تطوير منتجات البرمجيات مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","دلائل لتحديد مواصفات المنتج","تخطيط التنفيذ مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","وثائق فنية لأدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديلات لأدوات تطوير البرمجيات","كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لتطوير البرمجيات","ما هي أداة مواصفات المنتج","أداة مواصفات المنتج مقابل أدوات أخرى"]}},"owner":"benjaminshoemaker","repo":"ai_coding_project_base","repoPath":"benjaminshoemaker/ai_coding_project_base","stars":32,"forks":4,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T18:47:00Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"product-spec","description":"Generate PRODUCT_SPEC.md through guided Q&A. Use as the first step when starting a new greenfield project.","bodyPreview":"Generate a product specification document for the current project.\n\n## Workflow\n\nCopy this checklist and track progress:\n\n```\nProduct Spec Progress:\n- [ ] Step 1: Directory guard\n- [ ] Step 2: Project root confirmation\n- [ ] Step 3: Check for existing PRODUCT_SPEC.md\n- [ ] Step 4: Conduct guided Q&A with user\n- [ ] Step 5: Write PRODUCT_SPEC.md\n- [ ] Step 6: Handle deferred decisions\n- [ ] Step 7: Review and refine with user\n- [ ] Step 8: Suggest next step (/technical-spec)\n```\n\n## Directory Gua","body":"Generate a product specification document for the current project.\n\n## Workflow\n\nCopy this checklist and track progress:\n\n```\nProduct Spec Progress:\n- [ ] Step 1: Directory guard\n- [ ] Step 2: Project root confirmation\n- [ ] Step 3: Check for existing PRODUCT_SPEC.md\n- [ ] Step 4: Conduct guided Q&A with user\n- [ ] Step 5: Write PRODUCT_SPEC.md\n- [ ] Step 6: Handle deferred decisions\n- [ ] Step 7: Review and refine with user\n- [ ] Step 8: Suggest next step (/technical-spec)\n```\n\n## Directory Guard\n\n1. If `.toolkit-marker` exists in the current working directory → **STOP**:\n   \"You''re in the toolkit repo. Run this from your project directory instead:\n    `cd ~/Projects/your-project && /product-spec`\"\n\n## Project Root Confirmation\n\nBefore generating any files, confirm the output location with the user:\n\n```\nWill write PRODUCT_SPEC.md to: {absolute path of cwd}/\nContinue? (Yes / Change directory)\n```\n\nIf the user says \"Change directory\", ask for the correct path and instruct them to `cd` there first.\n\n## Existing File Guard (Prevent Overwrite)\n\nBefore asking any questions, check whether `PRODUCT_SPEC.md` already exists in the current directory.\n\n- If it does not exist: continue normally.\n- If it exists: **STOP** and ask the user what to do:\n  1. **Backup then overwrite (recommended)**: read the existing file and write it to `PRODUCT_SPEC.md.bak.YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS`, then write the new document to `PRODUCT_SPEC.md`\n  2. **Overwrite**: replace `PRODUCT_SPEC.md` with the new document\n  3. **Abort**: do not write anything; suggest they rename/move the existing file first\n\n## Process\n\nRead `.claude/skills/product-spec/PROMPT.md` and follow its instructions exactly:\n\n1. Ask the user to describe their idea\n2. Work through each question category (Problem, Users, Experience, Features, Data)\n3. Make recommendations with confidence levels\n4. Generate the final PRODUCT_SPEC.md document\n\n## Output\n\nWrite the completed specification to `PRODUCT_SPEC.md` in the current directory.\n\nAfter writing PRODUCT_SPEC.md, verify the file exists and is non-empty by reading the first few lines. If the file was not created successfully, report the error and retry.\n\n## Deferred Requirements Capture (During Q&A)\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Capture deferred requirements interactively during the Q&A process, not after.\n\n### When to Trigger\n\nDuring the Q&A, watch for signals that the user is deferring a requirement:\n- \"out of scope\"\n- \"not for MVP\" / \"post-MVP\"\n- \"v2\" / \"version 2\" / \"future\"\n- \"later\" / \"eventually\"\n- \"maybe\" / \"nice to have\"\n- \"we''ll skip that for now\"\n- \"not right now\"\n- \"that''s a separate thing\"\n\n### Capture Flow\n\nWhen you detect a deferral signal, immediately use AskUserQuestion:\n\n```\nQuestion: \"Would you like to save this to your deferred requirements?\"\nHeader: \"Defer?\"\nOptions:\n  - \"Yes, capture it\" — I''ll ask a few quick questions to document it\n  - \"No, skip\" — Don''t record this\n```\n\n**If user selects \"Yes, capture it\":**\n\nAsk these clarifying questions (can be combined into one AskUserQuestion with multiple questions):\n\n1. **What''s being deferred?**\n   \"In one sentence, what''s the requirement or feature?\"\n   (Pre-fill with your understanding from context)\n\n2. **Why defer it?**\n   Options: \"Out of scope for MVP\" / \"Needs more research\" / \"V2 feature\" / \"Resource constraints\" / \"Other\"\n\n3. **Notes for later?**\n   \"Any context that will help when revisiting this?\"\n   (Optional — user can skip)\n\n### Write to DEFERRED.md Immediately\n\nAfter collecting answers, append to `DEFERRED.md` right away (don''t wait until end).\n\n**If file doesn''t exist, create it:**\n\n```markdown\n# Deferred Requirements\n\n> Captured during specification Q&A. Review when planning future versions.\n\n## From PRODUCT_SPEC.md ({date})\n\n| Requirement | Reason | Notes |\n|-------------|--------|-------|\n| {user''s answer} | {selected reason} | {notes or \"—\"} |\n```\n\n**If file exists, append:**\n\n```markdown\n| {user''s answer} | {selected reason} | {notes or \"—\"} |\n```\n\n(If appending to a different spec''s section, add a new section header first.)\n\n### Continue Q&A\n\nAfter capturing (or skipping), continue the spec Q&A where you left off. Don''t break the flow.\n\n## Cross-Model Review (Automatic)\n\nAfter writing PRODUCT_SPEC.md, run cross-model review if Codex CLI is available:\n\n1. Check if Codex CLI is installed: `codex --version`\n2. If available, run `/codex-consult` on the generated document\n3. Present any findings to the user before proceeding\n\n**Consultation invocation:**\n```\n/codex-consult --research \"product requirements, user stories\" PRODUCT_SPEC.md\n```\n\n**If Codex finds issues:**\n- Show critical issues and recommendations\n- Ask user: \"Address findings before proceeding?\" (Yes/No)\n- If Yes: Apply suggested fixes\n- If No: Continue with noted issues\n\n**If Codex unavailable:** Skip silently and proceed to Next Step.\n\n## Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| PROMPT.md not found at `.claude/skills/product-spec/PROMPT.md` | Stop and report \"Skill asset missing — reinstall toolkit or run /setup\" |\n| DEFERRED.md write fails (permissions or disk) | Output deferred items to terminal, warn user, continue with spec generation |\n| Codex CLI invocation fails or times out | Log the error, skip cross-model review, proceed to Next Step |\n\n## Next Step\n\nWhen complete, inform the user:\n```\nPRODUCT_SPEC.md created at ./PRODUCT_SPEC.md\nDeferred Requirements: {count} items captured to DEFERRED.md\nCross-Model Review: PASSED | PASSED WITH NOTES | SKIPPED\n\nNext: Run /technical-spec\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:31:35.372Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Coding Assistants needing structured product specification generation.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化产品规格生成的 AI 编程助手。","ja":"構造化された製品仕様生成を必要とする AI コーディングアシスタントに最適です。","ko":"구조화된 제품 사양 생성이 필요한 AI 코딩 어시스턴트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para asistentes de codificación de IA que necesitan generación de especificaciones de producto estructuradas.","fr":"Idéal pour les assistants de codage IA nécessitant une génération de spécifications de produit structurées.","de":"Perfekt für AI-Coding-Assistenten, die eine strukturierte Generierung von Produktspezifikationen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Assistentes de Codificação de IA que necessitam de geração estruturada de especificações de produto.","ru":"Идеально подходит для ИИ-ассистентов по кодированию, которым требуется структурированное создание спецификаций продукта.","ar":"مثالي لمساعدات الذكاء الاصطناعي في البرمجة التي تحتاج إلى إنشاء مواصفات منتج منظمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate comprehensive product specification documents using guided Q&A sessions, producing executable documents in Markdown format, and handling deferred decisions for technical design and implementation planning.","zh":"赋能 Agent 通过引导式 Q&A 会话生成全面的产品规格文档，生成 Markdown 格式的可执行文档，并处理技术设计和实施规划中的延迟决策。","ja":"ガイド付き Q&A セッションを使用して包括的な製品仕様書を生成し、Markdown 形式の実行可能なドキュメントを作成し、技術設計と実装計画のための延期された決定を処理するように Agent を強化します。","ko":"지시형 Q&A 세션을 사용하여 포괄적인 제품 사양 문서를 생성하고, Markdown 형식의 실행 가능한 문서를 생성하며, 기술 설계 및 구현 계획을 위한 지연된 결정을 처리하도록 Agent에 권한을 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar documentos de especificación de producto completos utilizando sesiones de preguntas y respuestas guiadas, produciendo documentos ejecutables en formato Markdown y manejando decisiones diferidas para la planificación del diseño y la implementación técnica.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des documents de spécification de produit complets en utilisant des sessions de questions et réponses guidées, produisant des documents exécutables au format Markdown et gérant les décisions différées pour la planification de la conception et de la mise en œuvre technique.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, umfassende Produktspezifikationsdokumente mithilfe von guidierten Q&A-Sitzungen zu generieren, ausführbare Dokumente im Markdown-Format zu produzieren und aufgeschobene Entscheidungen für die technische Entwurfs- und Implementierungsplanung zu bearbeiten.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a gerar documentos abrangentes de especificação de produto usando sessões guiadas de perguntas e respostas, produzindo documentos executáveis em formato Markdown e lidando com decisões adiadas para planejamento técnico de design e implementação.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать комплексные документы спецификации продукта с помощью управляемых сессий вопросов и ответов, генерируя исполняемые документы в формате Markdown и обрабатывая отложенные решения для технического проектирования и планирования реализации.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء مستندات مواصفات منتج شاملة باستخدام جلسات الأسئلة والأجوبة الموجهة، وإنتاج مستندات قابلة للتنفيذ بصيغة Markdown، والتعامل مع القرارات المؤجلة للتخطيط التقني للتصميم والتنفيذ."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating product specification document generation","Conducting guided Q&A sessions for project planning","Generating PRODUCT_SPEC.md files for AI-executable projects"],"zh":["自动化产品规格文档生成","为项目规划进行引导式 Q&A 会话","为 AI 可执行项目生成 PRODUCT_SPEC.md 文件"],"ja":["製品仕様書の生成を自動化","プロジェクト計画のためのガイド付き Q&A セッションの実施","AI 実行可能プロジェクトのための PRODUCT_SPEC.md ファイルの生成"],"ko":["제품 사양 문서 생성 자동화","프로젝트 계획을 위한 지시형 Q&A 세션 수행","AI 실행 가능 프로젝트를 위한 PRODUCT_SPEC.md 파일 생성"],"es":["Automatización de la generación de documentos de especificación de producto","Realización de sesiones de preguntas y respuestas guiadas para la planificación de proyectos","Generación de archivos PRODUCT_SPEC.md para proyectos ejecutables por IA"],"fr":["Automatisation de la génération de documents de spécification de produit","Tenue de sessions de questions et réponses guidées pour la planification de projet","Génération de fichiers PRODUCT_SPEC.md pour les projets exécutables par IA"],"de":["Automatisierung der Generierung von Produktspezifikationsdokumenten","Durchführung von guidierten Q&A-Sitzungen für die Projektplanung","Generierung von PRODUCT_SPEC.md-Dateien für AI-ausführbare Projekte"],"pt":["Automatização da geração de documentos de especificação de produto","Realização de sessões guiadas de perguntas e respostas para planejamento de projetos","Geração de arquivos PRODUCT_SPEC.md para projetos executáveis por IA"],"ru":["Автоматизация создания документов спецификации продукта","Проведение управляемых сессий вопросов и ответов для планирования проектов","Создание файлов PRODUCT_SPEC.md для проектов, исполняемых ИИ"],"ar":["أتمتة إنشاء مستندات مواصفات المنتج","إجراء جلسات أسئلة وأجوبة موجهة لتخطيط المشاريع","إنشاء ملفات PRODUCT_SPEC.md للمشاريع القابلة للتنفيذ بواسطة الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires user input for Q&A sessions","Limited to generating PRODUCT_SPEC.md documents","Dependent on user review and refinement for accuracy"],"zh":["需要用户输入以进行 Q&A 会话","仅限于生成 PRODUCT_SPEC.md 文档","准确性依赖于用户的审查和优化"],"ja":["Q&A セッションにはユーザー入力が必要","PRODUCT_SPEC.md ドキュメントの生成に限定される","正確性はユーザーのレビューと改良に依存"],"ko":["Q&A 세션을 위한 사용자 입력 필요","PRODUCT_SPEC.md 문서 생성으로 제한됨","정확성을 위한 사용자 검토 및 개선에 의존"],"es":["Requiere entrada del usuario para sesiones de preguntas y respuestas","Limitado a la generación de documentos PRODUCT_SPEC.md","Dependiente de la revisión y refinamiento del usuario para la precisión"],"fr":["Nécessite une entrée utilisateur pour les sessions de questions et réponses","Limité à la génération de documents PRODUCT_SPEC.md","Dépend de l''examen et du raffinement de l''utilisateur pour l''exactitude"],"de":["Benutzereingabe für Q&A-Sitzungen erforderlich","Begrenzt auf die Generierung von PRODUCT_SPEC.md-Dokumenten","Von der Überprüfung und Verfeinerung durch den Benutzer für die Genauigkeit abhängig"],"pt":["Requer entrada do usuário para sessões de perguntas e respostas","Limitado à geração de documentos PRODUCT_SPEC.md","Dependente da revisão e refinamento do usuário para precisão"],"ru":["Требует ввода данных пользователем для сессий вопросов и ответов","Ограничено созданием документов PRODUCT_SPEC.md","Зависит от проверки и доработки пользователем для обеспечения точности"],"ar":["يتطلب مدخلات من المستخدم لجلسات الأسئلة والأجوبة","مقتصر على إنشاء مستندات PRODUCT_SPEC.md","يعتمد على مراجعة المستخدم وتحسينها للدقة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"05fc539236fc9e67b0e645059e03c6522ac7a7669043a3b7373f41dd7ace5f09","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('sfc-gh-dflippo/snowflake-dbt-demo/dbt-artifacts', 'community', 'sfc-gh-dflippo', 'snowflake-dbt-demo', 'sfc-gh-dflippo/snowflake-dbt-demo', 'dbt-artifacts', 28, 8, 65, '2026-02-19T20:02:32Z', '2026-02-26T13:19:56.989Z', 'd6606a67970176e314ad3f11e6542f75866c50179345ba159d92ec1040a5199e', '{"id":"sfc-gh-dflippo/snowflake-dbt-demo/dbt-artifacts","name":"dbt-artifacts","description":{"zh":"dbt-artifacts 项目展示了 dbt 在 Snowflake Data Cloud 中的众多功能，帮助开发者提高数据处理效率","ja":"dbt-artifacts プロジェクトは、Snowflake Data Cloud で dbt を使用する際の多くの機能を紹介します","ko":"dbt-artifacts 프로젝트는 Snowflake Data Cloud 에서 dbt 를 사용할 때 다양한 기능을 제공합니다","es":"dbt-artifacts demuestra las características de dbt con Snowflake Data Cloud para desarrolladores","fr":"dbt-artifacts démontre les fonctionnalités de dbt avec Snowflake Data Cloud pour les développeurs","de":"dbt-artifacts zeigt die Funktionen von dbt mit Snowflake Data Cloud für Entwickler","pt":"O dbt-artifacts é um projeto que demonstra recursos do dbt com a Snowflake Data Cloud. Aprenda a usar essas ferramentas para melhorar a produtividade","ru":"dbt-artifacts - это проект, демонстрирующий возможности dbt с Snowflake Data Cloud. Узнайте, как использовать эти ИИ Агенты для повышения производительности","ar":"dbt-artifacts هو مشروع يظهر العديد من الميزات الخاصة بقاعدة البيانات dbt مع سحابة البيانات Snowflake. تعلم استخدام هذه الأدوات لتحسين الإنتاجية","en":"This project demonstrates many of dbt''s features when used with the Snowflake Data Cloud"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理 dbt-artifacts：Snowflake 数据云集成","ja":"AIエージェント dbt-artifacts：Snowflake Data Cloud を使用した dbt の機能","ko":"AI 에이전트 dbt-artifacts: Snowflake Data Cloud 와의 통합","es":"Herramientas de IA: dbt-artifacts para Snowflake","fr":"Outils d''IA: dbt-artifacts pour Snowflake Data Cloud","de":"KI-Tools: dbt-artifacts für Snowflake Data Cloud","pt":"Ferramentas de IA: dbt-artifacts para Snowflake","ru":"ИИ Агенты: dbt-artifacts для Snowflake Data Cloud","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: dbt-artifacts للبيانات السحابية S...","en":"dbt-artifacts"},"description":{"zh":"dbt-artifacts 项目展示了 dbt 在 Snowflake Data Cloud 中的众多功能，帮助开发者提高数据处理效率","ja":"dbt-artifacts プロジェクトは、Snowflake Data Cloud で dbt を使用する際の多くの機能を紹介します","ko":"dbt-artifacts 프로젝트는 Snowflake Data Cloud 에서 dbt 를 사용할 때 다양한 기능을 제공합니다","es":"dbt-artifacts demuestra las características de dbt con Snowflake Data Cloud para desarrolladores","fr":"dbt-artifacts démontre les fonctionnalités de dbt avec Snowflake Data Cloud pour les développeurs","de":"dbt-artifacts zeigt die Funktionen von dbt mit Snowflake Data Cloud für Entwickler","pt":"O dbt-artifacts é um projeto que demonstra recursos do dbt com a Snowflake Data Cloud. Aprenda a usar essas ferramentas para melhorar a produtividade","ru":"dbt-artifacts - это проект, демонстрирующий возможности dbt с Snowflake Data Cloud. Узнайте, как использовать эти ИИ Агенты для повышения производительности","ar":"dbt-artifacts هو مشروع يظهر العديد من الميزات الخاصة بقاعدة البيانات dbt مع سحابة البيانات Snowflake. تعلم استخدام هذه الأدوات لتحسين الإنتاجية","en":"This project demonstrates many of dbt''s features when used with the Snowflake Data Cloud"},"definition":{"en":"This project demonstrates many of dbt''s features when used with the Snowflake Data Cloud"},"features":{"zh":["展示 dbt 的强大功能","Snowflake Data Cloud 集成","提高数据处理效率","支持多种数据源","提供详细的文档和示例"],"ja":["dbt の強力な機能を紹介","Snowflake Data Cloud との統合","データ処理の効率を向上させる","複数のデータソースをサポート","詳細なドキュメントとサンプルを提供"],"ko":["dbt 의 강력한 기능을 제공","Snowflake Data Cloud 와의 통합","데이터 처리 능력을 높여줌","다양한 데이터 소스를 지원","상세한 문서와 예제를 제공"],"es":["Integración con Snowflake Data Cloud","Demostración de características de dbt","Uso de dbt para desarrolladores","Funcionalidades de dbt con Snowflake","Desarrollo de proyectos con dbt-artifacts"],"fr":["Intégration avec Snowflake Data Cloud","Démo des fonctionnalités de dbt","Utilisation de dbt pour les développeurs","Fonctionnalités de dbt avec Snowflake","Développement de projets avec dbt-artifacts"],"de":["Integration mit Snowflake Data Cloud","Demonstration von dbt-Funktionen","Verwendung von dbt für Entwickler","Funktionen von dbt mit Snowflake","Entwicklung von Projekten mit dbt-artifacts"],"pt":["Demonstração de recursos do dbt","Integração com a Snowflake Data Cloud","Melhoria da produtividade","Otimização de dados","Fácil implementação"],"ru":["Демонстрация возможностей dbt","Интеграция с Snowflake Data Cloud","Повышение производительности","Оптимизация данных","Лёгкая реализация"],"ar":["إظهار الميزات الخاصة بقاعدة البيانات dbt","التكامل مع سحابة البيانات Snowflake","تحسين الإنتاجية","تحسين البيانات","طرق تنفيذ بسيطة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["dbt 教程","Snowflake Data Cloud 集成","数据处理效率","dbt-artifacts 项目","AI 智能代理","数据云集成","how to use dbt","dbt vs Snowflake"],"ja":["dbt チュートリアル","Snowflake Data Cloud 統合","データ処理の効率","dbt-artifacts プロジェクト","AIエージェント","データクラウド統合","how to use dbt","dbt vs Snowflake"],"ko":["dbt 튜토리얼","Snowflake Data Cloud 통합","데이터 처리 능력","dbt-artifacts 프로젝트","AI 에이전트","데이터 클라우드 통합","how to use dbt","dbt vs Snowflake"],"es":["herramientas de ia para desarrolladores","dbt-artifacts tutorial","snowflake data cloud alternativa","dbt vs snowflake","cómo instalar dbt-artifacts","guía de configuración de dbt","desarrollo de proyectos con dbt","dbt-artifacts características"],"fr":["outils d''ia pour développeurs","tutoriel dbt-artifacts","alternative à snowflake data cloud","dbt vs snowflake","comment installer dbt-artifacts","guide de configuration de dbt","développement de projets avec dbt","caractéristiques de dbt-artifacts"],"de":["ki-tools für entwickler","dbt-artifacts tutorial","alternative zu snowflake data cloud","dbt vs snowflake","wie installiere ich dbt-artifacts","anleitung zur konfiguration von dbt","entwicklung von projekten mit dbt","funktionen von dbt-artifacts"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia","dbt artifacts","snowflake data cloud","como usar dbt","o que é dbt","dbt vs outras ferramentas","instalar dbt","guia de configuração dbt"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","dbt-artifacts","Snowflake Data Cloud","как использовать dbt","что такое dbt","dbt vs другие инструменты","установить dbt","руководство по настройке dbt"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","dbt-artifacts","سحابة البيانات Snowflake","كيفية استخدام dbt","ما هو dbt","dbt مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت dbt","دليل إعداد dbt"]}},"owner":"sfc-gh-dflippo","repo":"snowflake-dbt-demo","repoPath":"sfc-gh-dflippo/snowflake-dbt-demo","stars":28,"forks":8,"updatedAt":"2026-02-19T20:02:32Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dbt-artifacts","description":"","bodyPreview":"# dbt Artifacts Package - AI Instructions\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis skill enables AI agents to help users monitor dbt execution using the\nbrooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts package. The package captures detailed execution metadata during dbt\nruns and stores it in queryable tables for analysis and monitoring.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when users ask about:\n\n- Tracking test and model execution history\n- Analyzing dbt run patterns over time\n- Monitoring data quality metrics from dbt tests\n-","body":"# dbt Artifacts Package - AI Instructions\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis skill enables AI agents to help users monitor dbt execution using the\nbrooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts package. The package captures detailed execution metadata during dbt\nruns and stores it in queryable tables for analysis and monitoring.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nActivate this skill when users ask about:\n\n- Tracking test and model execution history\n- Analyzing dbt run patterns over time\n- Monitoring data quality metrics from dbt tests\n- Investigating dbt performance issues or slow models\n- Setting up execution logging and observability\n- Querying dbt execution metadata programmatically\n- Comparing dbt monitoring approaches (Artifacts vs Event Tables)\n\n## What dbt Artifacts Does\n\nThe package captures one row per dbt artifact execution (models, tests, seeds, snapshots) with:\n\n- **Execution status**: success, error, skipped, fail, warn\n- **Runtime metrics**: Duration, rows affected, compile time\n- **Test results**: Failure counts, error messages\n- **Run context**: Command, environment, dbt version, threading\n- **Dependencies**: Model lineage and relationships\n\n## Core Tables Reference\n\n| Table              | Purpose                   | Key Columns                                                             |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `invocations`      | One row per dbt run       | `command_invocation_id`, `dbt_command`, `target_name`, `run_started_at` |\n| `model_executions` | Model runtime performance | `status`, `total_node_runtime`, `rows_affected`, `materialization`      |\n| `test_executions`  | Data quality tracking     | `status`, `failures`, `total_node_runtime`, `message`                   |\n| `seeds`            | Seed file execution       | Similar to model_executions                                             |\n| `snapshots`        | Snapshot execution        | Similar to model_executions with SCD tracking                           |\n| `sources`          | Source freshness          | Freshness check results                                                 |\n| `exposures`        | Exposure execution        | Exposure dependencies                                                   |\n\n**Join Pattern**: Always join through `command_invocation_id` (links all executions in a run) and\n`node_id` (identifies specific artifact).\n\n## Installation & Setup\n\nWhen users need to install or configure dbt Artifacts:\n\n### Step 1: Add Package\n\nAdd to `packages.yml`:\n\n```yaml\npackages:\n  - package: brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts\n    version: 2.9.3\n```\n\n### Step 2: Configure Hook\n\nAdd to `dbt_project.yml`:\n\n```yaml\non-run-end:\n  - \"{{ dbt_artifacts.upload_results(results) }}\"\n\nmodels:\n  dbt_artifacts:\n    +database: your_database\n    +schema: dbt_artifacts\n```\n\n### Step 3: Install and Initialize\n\n```bash\ndbt deps\ndbt run --select dbt_artifacts\n```\n\nAfter first run, all subsequent dbt invocations automatically log results.\n\n## Helping Users with Queries\n\n### Query Strategy\n\nWhen users ask for monitoring queries:\n\n1. **Identify the goal**: What are they trying to monitor? (test failures, slow models, run history,\n   etc.)\n2. **Reference query library**: Point to relevant queries in the `scripts/` directory (see\n   **Monitoring Queries** section below)\n3. **Customize as needed**: Adjust date ranges, filters, thresholds\n4. **Explain results**: Help interpret the output and recommend actions\n\n### Common Query Patterns\n\nAll queries are available as individual executable scripts. See the **Monitoring Queries** section\nbelow for detailed descriptions and usage.\n\n### Query Best Practices\n\n**ALWAYS recommend these patterns:**\n\n- ✅ Filter by `run_started_at` with specific date range (performance)\n\n  ```sql\n  WHERE run_started_at >= DATEADD(day, -7, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP())\n  ```\n\n- ✅ Use `command_invocation_id` to link related executions efficiently\n- ✅ Filter `HAVING COUNT(*) >= 5` for meaningful aggregations\n- ✅ Join through both `command_invocation_id` AND `node_id` when linking metadata to executions\n\n**NEVER do these:**\n\n- ❌ Query entire table without date filtering\n\n  ```sql\n  -- BAD: Scans entire history\n  SELECT * FROM test_executions WHERE status = ''fail'';\n\n  -- GOOD: Filtered by date\n  SELECT * FROM test_executions\n  WHERE status = ''fail''\n    AND run_started_at >= DATEADD(day, -7, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP());\n  ```\n\n- ❌ Create alerts for every single test failure (too noisy)\n- ❌ Store more than 6 months without archival strategy\n\n### Storage Management\n\n**Archival Strategy (Quarterly):**\n\n```sql\n-- Archive data older than 90 days\nCREATE TABLE dbt_artifacts_archive.model_executions_2024_q4 AS\nSELECT *\nFROM dbt_artifacts.model_executions\nWHERE run_started_at < DATEADD(day, -90, CURRENT_DATE());\n\n-- Delete archived data from active tables\nDELETE FROM dbt_artifacts.model_executions\nWHERE run_started_at < DATEADD(day, -90, CURRENT_DATE());\n```\n\n**Storage Planning:**\n\n- Small project (50 models, 100 tests): ~1-5 MB/week\n- Medium project (200 models, 500 tests): ~10-20 MB/week\n- Large project (1000+ models, 2000+ tests): ~50-100 MB/week\n\nPlan for **1-2 GB per quarter** for medium projects.\n\n## Comparing Monitoring Approaches\n\nWhen users ask \"Should I use dbt Artifacts or Event Tables?\":\n\n### Use dbt Artifacts When\n\n**Cross-platform compatibility is critical:**\n\n- Running dbt from multiple platforms (dbt Cloud, local CLI, Airflow, etc.)\n- Need consistent monitoring across all execution environments\n- Team uses mixed deployment strategies\n\n**Historical analysis is primary goal:**\n\n- Analyzing trends over 30+ days\n- Long-term performance baseline tracking\n- Quarterly or annual reporting on dbt execution\n- Compliance or audit trail requirements\n\n**Running dbt outside Snowflake:**\n\n- Using dbt Cloud exclusively\n- Executing dbt from Airflow, Azure DevOps, GitHub Actions\n- Local development with dbt CLI\n- Any non-Snowflake execution environment\n\n**Programmatic access to metadata required:**\n\n- Building custom dashboards in BI tools\n- Integrating with existing observability platforms\n- Creating custom alerting logic\n- Feeding data to data catalogs or lineage tools\n\n**Delayed reporting is acceptable:**\n\n- Runs on `on-run-end` hook (after full execution completes)\n- Historical batch analysis vs real-time monitoring\n- End-of-run summaries are sufficient\n\n### Avoid dbt Artifacts When\n\n**Real-time monitoring is critical:**\n\n- Need immediate notification of failures\n- Want to see execution progress during runs\n- Require detailed trace spans and profiling → **Use**: dbt Projects on Snowflake Event Tables\n\n**Running exclusively in Snowflake:**\n\n- Using dbt PROJECT objects in Snowflake\n- Native Snowflake integration preferred\n- Want Snowflake-native telemetry → **Use**: dbt Projects Event Tables\n\n**Storage constraints exist:**\n\n- Limited database space for historical data\n- Can''t maintain growing execution history\n- No archival strategy in place → **Use**: Event Tables with shorter retention or external logging\n\n### Use Both for Comprehensive Monitoring\n\n**Recommended Architecture:**\n\n```sql\ndbt Artifacts (Historical)          Event Tables (Real-time)\n        ↓                                    ↓\nLong-term trends                   Immediate alerts\nQuarterly reports                  Live dashboards\nCross-platform metrics             Trace-level profiling\nBI tool integration               Native Snowflake tools\n```\n\n**Example:**\n\n1. **Event Tables**: Monitor active runs in real-time, alert on failures immediately\n2. **dbt Artifacts**: Analyze historical patterns, track monthly trends, feed BI dashboards\n\n### Comparison Matrix\n\n| Feature                   | dbt Artifacts             | dbt Projects Event Tables     |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| **Execution Environment** | Any (Cloud, CLI, Airflow) | Snowflake native only         |\n| **Telemetry Timing**      | On run completion (hook)  | Real-time during execution    |\n| **Historical Data**       | User-managed retention    | Configurable retention policy |\n| **Platform Integration**  | Cross-platform            | Snowflake-native              |\n| **Query Interface**       | Standard SQL tables       | Event table syntax            |\n| **Setup Complexity**      | Package + hook config     | dbt PROJECT configuration     |\n| **Trace Spans**           | No                        | Yes (detailed profiling)      |\n| **Best For**              | Historical analysis       | Real-time monitoring          |\n\n## Monitoring Queries\n\nIndividual SQL scripts for common monitoring tasks. Execute with Snowflake CLI:\n\n```sql\nsnow sql -f scripts/<query_file>.sql -c default\n```\n\n### Test Quality Monitoring\n\n**scripts/test_reliability_metrics.sql**\n\n- Calculate pass/fail rates to identify flaky tests\n- Shows failure percentages and execution times\n- Filters tests with 5+ executions for statistical relevance\n\n**scripts/recent_test_failures.sql**\n\n- Track test failures from last 7 days with full context\n- Includes run details, test names, and error messages\n- Useful for immediate troubleshooting\n\n**scripts/test_execution_trends.sql**\n\n- Daily test execution counts and pass/fail rates\n- Track test suite health over 30-day period\n- Identify patterns in test failures\n\n### Model Performance Monitoring\n\n**scripts/slowest_models.sql**\n\n- Identify top 20 slowest models by average runtime\n- Shows min/max/avg execution times and row counts\n- Filter models with 5+ executions\n\n**scripts/model_execution_errors.sql**\n\n- Recent model failures (last 7 days) with error messages\n- Includes model path and execution context\n- Helps identify recurring model issues\n\n**scripts/performance_regression_detection.sql**\n\n- Compare recent (7-day) vs baseline (30-day) performance\n- Alert on models with 20%+ slowdown\n- Calculate performance degradation percentage\n\n### Execution History\n\n**scripts/dbt_run_summary.sql**\n\n- High-level overview of all dbt runs (last 30 days)\n- Shows commands, targets, versions, and refresh flags\n- Useful for audit trails and pattern analysis\n\n## Common User Tasks\n\n### Task 1: \"Show me recent test failures\"\n\n1. Run: `snow sql -f scripts/recent_test_failures.sql -c default`\n2. Adjust date range if needed (default: last 7 days)\n3. Explain how to interpret `failures` column (0 = pass, >0 = fail)\n4. Suggest filtering by specific test names or models if needed\n\n### Task 2: \"Which models are slowest?\"\n\n1. Run: `snow sql -f scripts/slowest_models.sql -c default`\n2. Help identify if slowness is consistent (avg) or intermittent (max)\n3. Suggest investigating models > 5 minutes or 2x baseline\n4. Recommend materialization changes or optimization strategies\n\n### Task 3: \"Track test reliability over time\"\n\n1. Run: `snow sql -f scripts/test_reliability_metrics.sql -c default`\n2. Help identify flaky tests (failure_rate_pct between 10-90%)\n3. Recommend investigating tests with 100% failure rate\n4. Suggest baseline: < 5% failure rate for healthy tests\n\n### Task 4: \"Set up dbt Artifacts\"\n\n1. Walk through 3-step installation (packages.yml → dbt_project.yml → dbt deps)\n2. Verify installation: `dbt run --select dbt_artifacts`\n3. Test logging: `dbt run` (any command) then query `invocations` table\n4. Recommend dedicated schema and archival strategy\n\n## Troubleshooting Common Issues\n\n| Issue                | Solution                                                                      |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| \"No data in tables\"  | Verify `on-run-end` hook in dbt_project.yml; run `dbt run` to trigger logging |\n| \"Tables not created\" | Run `dbt run --select dbt_artifacts` explicitly first                         |\n| \"Permission denied\"  | Ensure dbt user has CREATE/INSERT rights in target database/schema            |\n| \"Missing columns\"    | Update package: `dbt deps --upgrade` to latest version                        |\n| \"Slow queries\"       | Add date filter on `run_started_at`; consider archiving old data              |\n\n## Related Skills\n\n**Complementary Observability:**\n\n- `dbt-projects-on-snowflake` skill - For native Snowflake deployment with real-time event table\n  monitoring\n\n**When to use both together:**\n\n- **dbt Artifacts** for cross-platform monitoring and historical analysis across all dbt\n  environments\n- **dbt Projects on Snowflake** for real-time Snowflake-native monitoring with OpenTelemetry tracing\n\n**When to use one vs the other:**\n\n- Use **dbt Artifacts** alone if you run dbt outside Snowflake (dbt Cloud, Airflow, local)\n- Use **dbt Projects on Snowflake** alone if you exclusively run dbt within Snowflake\n- Use **both** for comprehensive enterprise monitoring (historical + real-time)\n\n---\n\n## Monitoring Best Practices\n\n### Test Quality Best Practices\n\n**Establish baselines:**\n\n- **Healthy**: Test failure rate < 5%\n- **Warning**: Test failure rate 5-10%\n- **Critical**: Test failure rate > 10%\n\n**Identify flaky tests:**\n\n- Failure rate between 10-90% (inconsistent results)\n- Recommend investigation or test refactoring\n\n**Alert on patterns:**\n\n- New test with 100% failure rate (incorrect test logic)\n- Previously stable test suddenly failing\n- Test execution time 2x+ baseline\n\n### Model Performance Best Practices\n\n**Performance thresholds:**\n\n- **Investigate**: Models consistently > 5 minutes\n- **Critical**: Runtime increase > 2x historical average\n- **Optimize**: Models in top 20 slowest\n\n**Alert strategies:**\n\n- High priority: Models with `status = ''error''`\n- Medium priority: Runtime increase > 50% from baseline\n- Low priority: Slow model trending (track over time)\n\n### Alerting Best Practices\n\n**High Priority (Immediate Action):**\n\n- Test status = ''fail'' or ''error''\n- Model status = ''error''\n- Critical model runtime > 2x baseline\n- Production environment failures\n\n**Medium Priority (Investigation Within 24h):**\n\n- Test status = ''warn''\n- Model skipped > 10% of runs\n- Runtime increase > 50% from baseline\n- Unusual invocation patterns\n\n**Low Priority (Track Trends):**\n\n- Slow model performance (not critical path)\n- Test success rate slowly declining\n- Incremental drift in execution duration\n\n---\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- **SQL Scripts**: `scripts/` - Individual query files ready to execute with Snowflake CLI\n- **Package Documentation**:\n  [brooklyn-data.github.io/dbt_artifacts](https://brooklyn-data.github.io/dbt_artifacts)\n- **GitHub Repository**:\n  [github.com/brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts](https://github.com/brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T13:19:56.989Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing advanced dbt execution monitoring and metadata analysis capabilities with Snowflake Data Cloud","zh":"非常适合需要高级dbt执行监控和元数据分析能力的数据分析代理，特别是与Snowflake Data Cloud集成时","ja":"Snowflake Data Cloudを使用するデータ分析エージェントに適しており、高度なdbt実行監視とメタデータ分析機能が必要な場合に最適です","ko":"스노우플레이크 데이터 클라우드와의 통합 시 고급 dbt 실행 모니터링 및 메타데이터 분석 기능이 필요한 데이터 분석 에이전트에게 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan capacidades de monitoreo de ejecución de dbt avanzadas y análisis de metadatos con Snowflake Data Cloud","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données nécessitant un suivi avancé de l''exécution de dbt et des capacités d''analyse de métadonnées avec Snowflake Data Cloud","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die erweiterte dbt-Ausführungsüberwachung und Metadatenanalysefunktionen mit Snowflake Data Cloud benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de monitoramento avançado de execução dbt e capacidades de análise de metadados com Snowflake Data Cloud","ru":"Идеально подходит для Агентов Анализа Данных, которым необходимы передовые возможности мониторинга выполнения dbt и анализа метаданных с Snowflake Data Cloud","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء تحليل البيانات الذين يحتاجون إلى مراقبة متقدمة للتشغيل dbt وقدرات تحليل البيانات الوصفية مع Snowflake Data Cloud"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to capture detailed execution metadata during dbt runs, storing it in queryable tables for analysis and monitoring using the brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts package, enabling advanced data quality metric tracking and dbt run pattern analysis","zh":"赋予代理捕获dbt运行期间的详细执行元数据的能力，并将其存储在可查询的表中，用于分析和监控，实现高级数据质量指标跟踪和dbt运行模式分析，所有这些都通过brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts包实现","ja":"エージェントがdbtの実行中に詳細な実行メタデータを取得し、分析や監視に使用できるテーブルに保存できるようにし、brooklyn-data/dbt_artifactsパッケージを使用して高度なデータ品質メトリックの追跡やdbt実行パターンの分析を可能にします","ko":"에이전트가 dbt 실행 중에 자세한 실행 메타데이터를 캡처하여 분석 및 모니터링에 사용할 수 있는 테이블에 저장할 수 있도록 하여, brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts 패키지를 사용하여 고급 데이터 품질 메트릭 추적 및 dbt 실행 패턴 분석을 가능하게 합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a capturar metadatos de ejecución detallados durante las ejecuciones de dbt, almacenándolos en tablas consultables para análisis y monitoreo utilizando el paquete brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts, lo que permite un seguimiento avanzado de métricas de calidad de datos y análisis de patrones de ejecución de dbt","fr":"Permet aux agents de capturer des métadonnées d''exécution détaillées lors des exécutions de dbt, les stockant dans des tables consultables pour analyse et surveillance en utilisant le paquet brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts, permettant ainsi un suivi avancé des métriques de qualité des données et l''analyse des modèles d''exécution de dbt","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, detaillierte Ausführungsmetadaten während dbt-Läufen zu erfassen und sie in abfragbaren Tabellen für Analyse und Überwachung mit dem Paket brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts zu speichern, wodurch ein erweitertes Tracking von Datenqualitätsmetriken und eine Analyse von dbt-Ausführungsmustern ermöglicht wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a capturar metadados de execução detalhados durante execuções dbt, armazenando-os em tabelas consultáveis para análise e monitoramento usando o pacote brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts, permitindo o acompanhamento avançado de métricas de qualidade de dados e análise de padrões de execução dbt","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью захватить подробные метаданные выполнения во время запусков dbt, храня их в запросных таблицах для анализа и мониторинга с использованием пакета brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts, обеспечивая продвинутый отслеживание метрик качества данных и анализ закономерностей выполнения dbt","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على التقاط بيانات وصفية مفصلة خلال تشغيل dbt، وتخزينها في جداول قابلة للاستعلام للتحليل والمراقبة باستخدام حزمة brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts، مما يتيح تتبع متقدم لمقاييس جودة البيانات وتحليل أنماط تشغيل dbt"},"useCases":{"en":["Tracking test and model execution history","Analyzing dbt run patterns over time","Monitoring data quality metrics from dbt tests"],"zh":["跟踪测试和模型执行历史","随时间分析dbt运行模式","从dbt测试监控数据质量指标"],"ja":["テストとモデル実行履歴の追跡","時間経過によるdbt実行パターンの分析","dbtテストによるデータ品質メトリックの監視"],"ko":["테스트 및 모델 실행 기록 추적","시간 경과에 따른 dbt 실행 패턴 분석","dbt 테스트에서 데이터 품질 메트릭 모니터링"],"es":["Seguimiento del historial de ejecución de pruebas y modelos","Análisis de patrones de ejecución de dbt con el tiempo","Monitoreo de métricas de calidad de datos desde pruebas de dbt"],"fr":["Suivi de l''historique d''exécution des tests et des modèles","Analyse des modèles d''exécution de dbt au fil du temps","Surveillance des métriques de qualité des données à partir des tests de dbt"],"de":["Nachverfolgung der Ausführungshistorie von Tests und Modellen","Analyse von dbt-Ausführungsmustern im Laufe der Zeit","Überwachung von Datenqualitätsmetriken von dbt-Tests"],"pt":["Rastrear histórico de execução de testes e modelos","Analisar padrões de execução dbt ao longo do tempo","Monitorar métricas de qualidade de dados de testes dbt"],"ru":["Отслеживать историю выполнения тестов и моделей","Анализировать закономерности выполнения dbt со временем","Мониторить метрики качества данных из тестов dbt"],"ar":["تتبع سجل تشغيل الاختبارات والنماذج","تحليل أنماط تشغيل dbt مع مرور الوقت","مراقبة مقاييس جودة البيانات من اختبارات dbt"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Snowflake Data Cloud setup","Dependent on brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts package"],"zh":["需要Snowflake Data Cloud设置","依赖brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts包"],"ja":["Snowflake Data Cloudのセットアップが必要","brooklyn-data/dbt_artifactsパッケージに依存"],"ko":["스노우플레이크 데이터 클라우드 설정이 필요","brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts 패키지에 의존"],"es":["Requiere configuración de Snowflake Data Cloud","Dependiente del paquete brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de Snowflake Data Cloud","Dépendant du paquet brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts"],"de":["Benötigt eine Einrichtung von Snowflake Data Cloud","Abhängig vom Paket brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts"],"pt":["Requer configuração do Snowflake Data Cloud","Depende do pacote brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts"],"ru":["Требует настройки Snowflake Data Cloud","Зависит от пакета brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد Snowflake Data Cloud","يعتمد على حزمة brooklyn-data/dbt_artifacts"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d6606a67970176e314ad3f11e6542f75866c50179345ba159d92ec1040a5199e","qualityScore":65}');
