daptabilidad a casos de uso específicos"],"fr":["Approche flexible de DDD","Conception de domaine orientée développeurs","Implémentation de TypeScript","Intégration avec CellixJS","Adaptabilité à des cas d''utilisation spécifiques"],"de":["Flexible Ansatz für DDD","Domänen-Design orientiert an Entwickler","Implementierung von TypeScript","Integration mit CellixJS","Anpassungsfähigkeit an spezifische Anwendungsfälle"],"pt":["Abordagem flexível e opinada para DDD","Adaptação rápida ao caso de uso específico","Desenvolvimento com TypeScript","Integração com Domain Driven Design","Ferramenta de IA para devs"],"ru":["Гибкий и ограниченный подход к DDD","Быстрая адаптация к конкретному случаю","Разработка на TypeScript","Интеграция с Domain Driven Design","ИИ Агент для разработчиков"],"ar":["نهج مرن وملائم لتصميم الدومين","تحويل سريع إلى حالة استخدام محددة","التطوير باستخدام TypeScript","التكامل مع تصميم الدومين","أداة ذكاء اصطناعي للمطورين"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用 madr-enforcement","什么是 Domain Driven Design","madr-enforcement 替代方案","madr-enforcement vs 其他工具","madr-enforcement 安装","madr-enforcement 设置指南","TypeScript开发","Domain Driven Design 实践","AI 技能"],"ja":["madr-enforcement の使用方法","ドメイン駆動設計とは","madr-enforcement の代替","madr-enforcement と他のツールの比較","madr-enforcement のインストール","madr-enforcement の設定ガイド","TypeScript開発","ドメイン駆動設計の実践","AI スキル"],"ko":["madr-enforcement 사용법","도메인 주도 설계란","madr-enforcement 대안","madr-enforcement와 다른 툴의 비교","madr-enforcement 설치","madr-enforcement 설정 가이드","TypeScript 개발","도메인 주도 설계 실践","AI 스킬"],"es":["herramientas de inteligencia artificial","ddd ejemplo","domain driven design","typescript","cómo usar CellixJS","alternativas a CellixJS","instalación de CellixJS"],"fr":["outils d''intelligence artificielle","exemple ddd","conception de domaine pilotée","typescript","comment utiliser CellixJS","alternatives à CellixJS","installation de CellixJS"],"de":["ki-tools","ddd-beispiel","domain-getriebenes design","typescript","wie man CellixJS verwendet","alternativen zu CellixJS","installation von CellixJS"],"pt":["como usar Madr-Enforcement","o que é Domain Driven Design","Madr-Enforcement alternativa","Madr-Enforcement vs outros","instalar Madr-Enforcement","guia de configuração do Madr-Enforcement","desenvolvimento com TypeScript","ferramentas de IA para devs"],"ru":["как использовать Madr-Enforcement","что такое Domain Driven Design","альтернатива Madr-Enforcement","Madr-Enforcement vs другие","установить Madr-Enforcement","руководство по настройке Madr-Enforcement","разработка на TypeScript","ИИ Агенты для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Madr-Enforcement","ما هو تصميم الدومين","بديل Madr-Enforcement","Madr-Enforcement مقابل أخرى","تثبيت Madr-Enforcement","دليل إعداد Madr-Enforcement","التطوير باستخدام TypeScript","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين"]}},"owner":"CellixJs","repo":"cellixjs","repoPath":"CellixJs/cellixjs","stars":16,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-10T14:45:50Z","topics":["ddd","ddd-example","domain-driven-design","typescript"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"madr-enforcement","description":">","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# MADR Enforcement Skill\n\nThis skill ensures that code written in the CellixJS project adheres to the architectural standards, patterns, \nand guidelines documented in our Markdown Any Decision Records (MADRs). All ADRs are located in \n`apps/docs/docs/decisions/` and represent binding architectural decisions that must be followed.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n\n- **Writing new code** - Ensure it follows established architectural patterns from ADRs\n- **Reviewing pull requests**","body":"# MADR Enforcement Skill\n\nThis skill ensures that code written in the CellixJS project adheres to the architectural standards, patterns, \nand guidelines documented in our Markdown Any Decision Records (MADRs). All ADRs are located in \n`apps/docs/docs/decisions/` and represent binding architectural decisions that must be followed.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when:\n\n- **Writing new code** - Ensure it follows established architectural patterns from ADRs\n- **Reviewing pull requests** - Verify code compliance with documented standards\n- **Refactoring existing code** - Align implementations with current ADRs\n- **Adding dependencies** - Check against technology choices documented in ADRs\n- **Making design decisions** - Verify alignment or identify need for new ADR\n- **Implementing features** - Follow patterns from relevant domain/infrastructure ADRs\n\n## CellixJS Architectural Decisions (ADRs)\n\nAll architectural decisions are documented in `apps/docs/docs/decisions/`. The following ADRs define \nstandards that **MUST** be enforced in code:\n\n### Architecture & Design Patterns\n\n#### ADR-0003: Domain-Driven Design (DDD)\n\n**Standards to Enforce:**\n\n1. **Bounded Contexts** - Code must be organized by bounded context\n   - Location: `packages/ocom/domain/contexts/{context-name}/`\n   - Each context has its own ubiquitous language\n   \n2. **Entity Structure** - Entities must follow DDD patterns\n   - File: `{entity}.ts`\n   - Must have unique identity (ID)\n   - Contains business logic methods\n   - Props interface defines state\n   \n3. **Value Objects** - Immutable objects defined by their values\n   - File: `{entity}.value-objects.ts`\n   - Must be immutable\n   - Use `@lucaspaganini/value-objects` framework\n   \n4. **Aggregate Roots** - Entry points for entity clusters\n   - File: `{entity}.ts` (aggregate root entities)\n   - Enforces business rules for the aggregate\n   - Guards integrity of related entities\n   \n5. **Unit of Work Pattern** - Atomic operations on domain models\n   - File: `{entity}.uow.ts`\n   - Transaction boundary for persistence\n   - One per aggregate root\n\n6. **Layer Separation**\n   - **Domain Layer**: Business logic only, no infrastructure\n   - **Application Service Layer**: Orchestration, coordinates use cases\n   - **Infrastructure Service Layer**: External systems, third-party APIs\n\n**Code Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] Is code organized by bounded context?\n- [ ] Do entities have unique identifiers?\n- [ ] Are value objects immutable?\n- [ ] Are aggregate boundaries respected?\n- [ ] Is domain logic separate from infrastructure?\n- [ ] Are Unit of Work patterns used for persistence?\n\n#### ADR-0019: MonoRepo and Turborepo\n\n**Standards to Enforce:**\n\n1. **Package Organization**\n   - Workspace structure defined in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`\n   - Package naming: `@ocom/*` or `@cellix/*`\n   \n2. **Build System**\n   - Use Turborepo for builds: `pnpm run build`\n   - Respect package dependencies\n   - Use affected builds: `pnpm run build:affected`\n   \n3. **Testing**\n   - Package-level tests in each workspace\n   - Use `pnpm run test:affected`\n   - Coverage reports per package\n\n**Code Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] Is new code in the correct workspace package?\n- [ ] Are package dependencies declared in package.json?\n- [ ] Do build scripts use Turborepo commands?\n- [ ] Are tests co-located with the code they test?\n\n### Code Quality & Standards\n\n#### ADR-0012: Biome for Linting\n\n**Standards to Enforce:**\n\n1. **Linting and Formatting**\n   - Use Biome (not ESLint or Prettier)\n   - Configuration in `biome.json`\n   - Run before commits: `pnpm run lint`\n   \n2. **Type Safety**\n   - Biome provides type-aware linting\n   - Strict TypeScript configuration\n   - No `any` types without justification\n   \n3. **Code Style**\n   - Tab indentation (per biome.json)\n   - Follow Biome''s formatting rules\n   - Auto-fix with `pnpm run format`\n\n**Code Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] Does code pass Biome linting?\n- [ ] Is code formatted with Biome?\n- [ ] Are TypeScript types strict and complete?\n- [ ] No ESLint or Prettier configurations added?\n\n#### ADR-0013: Test Suite Architecture\n\n**Standards to Enforce:**\n\n1. **Test Framework**\n   - Use Vitest for unit tests\n   - Test coverage via `pnpm run test:coverage`\n   \n2. **Test Organization**\n   - Unit tests: Co-located with source files\n   - Integration tests: Separate directory\n   - E2E tests: SerenityJS (ADR-0007)\n   \n3. **Coverage Requirements**\n   - Coverage reports in `packages/*/coverage/`\n   - Minimum coverage thresholds enforced\n\n**Code Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] Are unit tests written for new code?\n- [ ] Do tests use Vitest framework?\n- [ ] Is test coverage adequate?\n- [ ] Are tests co-located appropriately?\n\n#### ADR-0022: Snyk Security Integration\n\n**Standards to Enforce:**\n\n1. **Security Scanning**\n   - Run Snyk before commits: `pnpm run snyk`\n   - Includes SAST (code), SCA (dependencies), IaC (Bicep)\n   \n2. **Vulnerability Management**\n   - Fix critical/high vulnerabilities immediately\n   - Document exceptions in `.snyk` file\n   - Get CODEOWNERS approval for ignores\n   \n3. **Workflow**\n   - Scan during development with `snyk_code_scan` MCP tool\n   - Verify fixes with re-scan\n   - Pass Snyk gate before commit\n\n**Code Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] Does code pass Snyk security scans?\n- [ ] Are vulnerabilities addressed or documented?\n- [ ] Are new dependencies scanned with `gh-advisory-database` MCP tool?\n- [ ] Are suppressed issues justified with expiration?\n\n### Infrastructure & Technology\n\n#### ADR-0002: OpenTelemetry\n\n**Standards to Enforce:**\n\n1. **Observability**\n   - Use `@azure/monitor-opentelemetry`\n   - Automatic instrumentation for MongoDB, Azure Functions\n   - GraphQL tracing via Apollo Server\n   \n2. **Integration**\n   - Package: `@ocom/service-otel`\n   - Configured via OpenTelemetry SDK\n\n**Code Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] Are new services instrumented with OpenTelemetry?\n- [ ] Is tracing configured for external calls?\n- [ ] Are metrics and logs properly structured?\n\n#### ADR-0011: Bicep for Infrastructure as Code\n\n**Standards to Enforce:**\n\n1. **IaC Language**\n   - Use Bicep (not ARM templates, Terraform)\n   - Location: `iac/` directory\n   \n2. **Resource Naming**\n   - Follow naming conventions in ADR-0021\n   - Use resource scoping strategy\n   \n3. **Deployment**\n   - Azure infrastructure deployments per ADR-0014\n   - CI/CD via Azure DevOps (ADR-0020)\n\n**Code Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] Is infrastructure defined in Bicep?\n- [ ] Do resource names follow conventions?\n- [ ] Are Bicep files scanned with Snyk IaC?\n\n#### ADR-0014: Azure Infrastructure Deployments\n\n**Standards to Enforce:**\n\n1. **Azure Functions**\n   - Version 4.x\n   - TypeScript runtime\n   - Registered via `cellix.registerAzureFunctionHandler()`\n   \n2. **Service Registration**\n   - Use `Cellix` class for DI orchestration\n   - Register services with `serviceRegistry.registerService()`\n   \n3. **Context Specification**\n   - Define context via `setContext()`\n   - Provide typed service access\n\n**Code Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] Are Azure Functions v4 patterns followed?\n- [ ] Is dependency injection used correctly?\n- [ ] Are services registered properly?\n\n### Technology Choices\n\n#### ADR-0004: Identity and Access Management\n#### ADR-0005: Authorization\n\n**Standards to Enforce:**\n\n1. **Authentication**\n   - Follow IAM patterns from ADR-0004\n   \n2. **Authorization**\n   - Implement authorization per ADR-0005\n\n**Code Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] Is authentication implemented correctly?\n- [ ] Are authorization checks in place?\n- [ ] Do security patterns match ADRs?\n\n#### ADR-0010: React Router Loaders\n\n**Standards to Enforce:**\n\n1. **Data Loading**\n   - Use React Router loaders for initial data\n   - Co-locate with route definitions\n   \n2. **UI Patterns**\n   - Loader functions return route data\n   - Components access via `useLoaderData()`\n\n**Code Review Checklist:**\n- [ ] Are loaders used for data fetching?\n- [ ] Is data loading co-located with routes?\n\n## Code Enforcement Workflow\n\n### When Writing New Code\n\n1. **Identify Relevant ADRs**\n   - Search `apps/docs/docs/decisions/` for applicable standards\n   - Read ADRs related to your domain, technology, or pattern\n   \n2. **Apply ADR Standards**\n   - Follow file naming conventions\n   - Use documented patterns\n   - Respect layer boundaries\n   \n3. **Verify Compliance**\n   - Run linting: `pnpm run lint`\n   - Run tests: `pnpm run test`\n   - Run security scan: `pnpm run snyk`\n   - Full verification: `pnpm run verify`\n\n### When Reviewing Code\n\n1. **Check ADR Alignment**\n   - Identify which ADRs apply to the changes\n   - Verify code follows documented patterns\n   \n2. **Common Violations**\n   - Domain logic in infrastructure layer (violates ADR-0003)\n   - Using ESLint instead of Biome (violates ADR-0012)\n   - Missing tests (violates ADR-0013)\n   - Unscanned dependencies (violates ADR-0022)\n   - Not using Bicep for infrastructure (violates ADR-0011)\n   \n3. **Request Changes**\n   - Reference specific ADR in review comments\n   - Explain which standard is violated\n   - Suggest corrective action\n\n### When Making Architectural Decisions\n\n1. **Check Existing ADRs**\n   - Search for related decisions\n   - Verify no conflicts with current ADRs\n   \n2. **Determine if New ADR Needed**\n   - New framework/library adoption → Requires ADR\n   - New architectural pattern → Requires ADR\n   - Infrastructure changes → Requires ADR\n   - Refactoring without architectural impact → No ADR needed\n   \n3. **Create ADR if Required**\n   - Follow process in ADR-0001\n   - Use templates in `apps/docs/docs/decisions/`\n   - Get approval from deciders before implementing\n\n## ADR Index by Category\n\n### Architecture & Design\n- **ADR-0003**: Domain-Driven Design (DDD)\n- **ADR-0019**: MonoRepo and Turborepo\n\n### Code Quality & Security\n- **ADR-0012**: Biome linting\n- **ADR-0013**: Test suite architecture\n- **ADR-0015**: SonarCloud integration\n- **ADR-0016**: SonarCloud code duplication\n- **ADR-0022**: Snyk security integration\n\n### Infrastructure & DevOps\n- **ADR-0002**: OpenTelemetry observability\n- **ADR-0011**: Bicep for IaC\n- **ADR-0014**: Azure infrastructure deployments\n- **ADR-0018**: Docusaurus Azure pipeline\n- **ADR-0020**: Azure DevOps monorepo pipeline\n- **ADR-0021**: Bicep resource scoping\n\n### Technology & Tools\n- **ADR-0004**: Identity and access management\n- **ADR-0005**: Authorization patterns\n- **ADR-0006**: Maps integration\n- **ADR-0007**: SerenityJS testing\n- **ADR-0008**: White-label architecture\n- **ADR-0009**: Cache purging\n- **ADR-0010**: React Router loaders\n- **ADR-0017**: Chrome content overrides\n- **ADR-0023**: TsGo migration\n\n### Process & Documentation\n- **ADR-0001**: MADR for architectural decisions\n\n## Common Code Patterns by ADR\n\n### DDD Pattern (ADR-0003)\n\n**Correct Implementation:**\n```typescript\n// packages/ocom/domain/contexts/user/user.ts\nexport interface UserProps {\n  readonly id: UserId;\n  readonly email: Email;\n  readonly profile: UserProfile;\n}\n\nexport class User implements AggregateRoot<UserProps> {\n  constructor(private props: UserProps) {}\n  \n  get id(): UserId { return this.props.id; }\n  \n  updateEmail(newEmail: Email): void {\n    // Domain logic here\n    this.props = { ...this.props, email: newEmail };\n  }\n  \n  // No database or infrastructure code here!\n}\n```\n\n**Incorrect Implementation (violates ADR-0003):**\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG: Domain entity with database code\nexport class User {\n  async save(): Promise<void> {\n    await mongoose.model(''User'').save(this); // Infrastructure in domain!\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Service Registration (ADR-0014)\n\n**Correct Implementation:**\n```typescript\n// Proper dependency injection\nCellix.initializeServices<ApiContextSpec>((serviceRegistry) => {\n  serviceRegistry.registerService(new ServiceMongoose(...));\n  serviceRegistry.registerService(new ServiceOtel(...));\n})\n.setContext((serviceRegistry) => ({ \n  domainDataSource: contextBuilder(serviceRegistry.getService(ServiceMongoose)),\n  telemetry: serviceRegistry.getService(ServiceOtel)\n}));\n```\n\n### Turborepo Usage (ADR-0019)\n\n**Correct Commands:**\n```bash\n# Build all packages\npnpm run build\n\n# Build only affected packages\npnpm run build:affected\n\n# Test with turbo caching\npnpm run test\n```\n\n**Incorrect:**\n```bash\n# ❌ WRONG: Building individual packages directly\ncd packages/ocom/domain && npm run build\n```\n\n## Enforcement During Code Generation\n\nWhen generating code:\n\n1. **Start with ADR Review**\n   - Identify applicable ADRs for the task\n   - Read relevant sections\n   \n2. **Generate Code Following Standards**\n   - Use patterns from ADRs\n   - Follow file naming conventions\n   - Respect layer boundaries\n   \n3. **Verify Compliance**\n   - Check code against ADR requirements\n   - Run verification suite\n   - Reference ADRs in comments if needed\n\n## References\n\n### Internal Documentation\n- **All ADRs**: `apps/docs/docs/decisions/`\n- **ADR-0001**: MADR Architecture Decisions (process for creating ADRs)\n- **ADR Templates**: `apps/docs/docs/decisions/adr-template.md`\n\n### External Resources\n- [MADR Project](https://adr.github.io/madr/)\n- [Domain-Driven Design](https://www.domainlanguage.com/ddd/)\n- [Biome Documentation](https://biomejs.dev/)\n- [Turborepo Documentation](https://turbo.build/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T13:11:00.947Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing adherence to architectural standards and patterns defined in Markdown Any Decision Records (MADRs)","zh":"非常适合需要遵守在 Markdown 中定义的任何决策记录（MADRs）中的架构标准和模式的代码审查代理","ja":"MADRsに定義されたアーキテクチャの標準とパターンに従う必要があるコードレビュー代理に最適","ko":"Markdown에 정의된 모든 의사 결정 레코드(MADRs)의 아키텍처 표준 및 패턴을 준수해야 하는 코드 리뷰 에이전트에게 완벽","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Revisión de Código que necesitan adherirse a estándares y patrones arquitectónicos definidos en Markdown Any Decision Records (MADRs)","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant le respect des normes et des modèles d''architecture définis dans Markdown Any Decision Records (MADRs)","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die die Einhaltung von architektonischen Standards und Mustern benötigen, die in Markdown Any Decision Records (MADRs) definiert sind","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam aderir a padrões e padrões arquitetônicos definidos em Registros de Decisões Markdown (MADRs)","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодового обзора, которым необходима соблюдение архитектурных стандартов и шаблонов, определенных в Markdown Any Decision Records (MADRs)","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء مراجعة الشفرة الذين يحتاجون إلى الالتزام بمعايير ونمط معماري محددة في سجلات قرارات Markdown (MADRs)"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce Domain Driven Design (DDD) principles and ensure code compliance with established architectural decisions documented in MADRs, leveraging CellixJS for flexible and opinionated development approaches, and integrating with Markdown files for decision records","zh":"赋予代理执行域驱动设计（DDD）原则的能力，并确保代码符合在MADRs中记录的已建立的架构决策，利用CellixJS进行灵活和有见解的开发方法，并与Markdown文件集成以记录决策","ja":"エージェントがドメイン駆動設計（DDD）原則を施行し、MADRsに記載された既存のアーキテクチャの決定に従ったコードを保証する機能を提供し、CellixJSを使用して柔軟で意見のある開発アプローチを実現し、Markdownファイルと統合して決定レコードを記録する","ko":"에이전트가 도메인 주도 설계(DDD) 원칙을 시행하고 MADRs에記載된既存의 아키텍처 결정과 일치하는 코드를 보장하는 기능을 제공하며, CellixJS를 사용하여 유연하고 의견이 있는 개발 접근 방식을 구현하고, Markdown 파일과 통합하여 의사 결정 기록을 기록","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar los principios de Domain Driven Design (DDD) y garantizar el cumplimiento del código con las decisiones arquitectónicas establecidas documentadas en MADRs, aprovechando CellixJS para enfoques de desarrollo flexibles y opinados, e integrándose con archivos de Markdown para registros de decisiones","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer les principes de Domain Driven Design (DDD) et de garantir la conformité du code avec les décisions d''architecture établies documentées dans les MADRs, en exploitant CellixJS pour des approches de développement flexibles et opinées, et en intégrant des fichiers Markdown pour les enregistrements de décision","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Prinzipien von Domain Driven Design (DDD) durchzusetzen und die Einhaltung des Codes mit den festgelegten architektonischen Entscheidungen zu gewährleisten, die in MADRs dokumentiert sind, indem CellixJS für flexible und voreingenommene Entwicklungsansätze genutzt wird und in Markdown-Dateien für Entscheidungsprotokolle integriert wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor princípios de Domain Driven Design (DDD) e garantir a conformidade do código com decisões arquitetônicas estabelecidas documentadas em MADRs, aproveitando o CellixJS para abordagens de desenvolvimento flexíveis e opinativas, e integrando com arquivos Markdown para registros de decisões","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать соблюдение принципов Domain Driven Design (DDD) и гарантировать соответствие кода установленным архитектурным решениям, задокументированным в MADRs, используя CellixJS для гибких и предвзятых подходов к разработке, и интегрируя с файлами Markdown для учета решений","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على فرض مبادئ Domain Driven Design (DDD) وضمان امتثال الشفرة للقرارات المعمارية المثبتة والموثقة في MADRs، مستفيدا من CellixJS للنُهج التطويرية المرنة والمؤثرة، وتكامل مع ملفات Markdown لسجلات القرارات"},"useCases":{"en":["Enforcing architectural standards in new code","Reviewing pull requests for MADR compliance","Validating code against established ADRs"],"zh":["在新代码中强制执行架构标准","审查拉取请求以确保MADR合规","验证代码是否与已建立的ADR一致"],"ja":["新しいコードでアーキテクチャの標準を施行する","MADRの準拠を確認するためにプルリクエストをレビューする","コードが既存のADRと一致することを検証する"],"ko":["새 코드에서 아키텍처 표준을 강제 실행","MADR 규정 준수를 확인하기 위해 풀 요청을 검토","코드가 이미 설정된 ADR와 일치하는지 확인"],"es":["Aplicar estándares arquitectónicos en nuevo código","Revisar solicitudes de extracción para el cumplimiento de MADR","Validar el código contra las ADR establecidas"],"fr":["Appliquer les normes d''architecture dans le nouveau code","Réviser les demandes d''extraction pour la conformité MADR","Valider le code par rapport aux ADR établies"],"de":["Architekturstandards in neuem Code durchsetzen","Zugriffsanfragen für die Einhaltung von MADR überprüfen","Code gegen festgelegte ADR überprüfen"],"pt":["Impor padrões arquitetônicos em novo código","Revisar solicitações de pull para conformidade com MADR","Validar código contra ADRs estabelecidas"],"ru":["Обеспечивать соблюдение архитектурных стандартов в новом коде","Проверять запросы на слияние для соответствия MADR","Проверять код на соответствие установленным ADR"],"ar":["فرض المعايير المعمارية في الشفرة الجديدة","مراجعة طلبات الدمج لامتثال MADR","التحقق من الشفرة ضد سجلات القرارات المثبتة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to MADR documents in `apps/docs/docs/decisions/` directory","Limited to CellixJS projects","Dependent on Markdown format for ADRs"],"zh":["需要访问`apps/docs/docs/decisions/`目录中的MADR文档","仅限CellixJS项目","依赖于Markdown格式的ADR"],"ja":["`apps/docs/docs/decisions/`ディレクトリ内のMADRドキュメントへのアクセスが必要","CellixJSプロジェクトのみ","Markdown形式のADRに依存"],"ko":["`apps/docs/docs/decisions/` 디렉토리 내의 MADR 문서에 대한 액세스가 필요","CellixJS 프로젝트만","Markdown 형식의 ADR에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso a los documentos MADR en el directorio `apps/docs/docs/decisions/`","Limitado a proyectos de CellixJS","Dependiente del formato Markdown para ADR"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux documents MADR dans le répertoire `apps/docs/docs/decisions/`","Limité aux projets CellixJS","Dépendant du format Markdown pour les ADR"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf MADR-Dokumente im Verzeichnis `apps/docs/docs/decisions/`","Begrenzt auf CellixJS-Projekte","Abhängig vom Markdown-Format für ADR"],"pt":["Requer acesso a documentos MADR no diretório `apps/docs/docs/decisions/`","Limitado a projetos CellixJS","Dependente do formato Markdown para ADRs"],"ru":["Требует доступа к документам MADR в директории `apps/docs/docs/decisions/`","Ограничен проектами CellixJS","Зависит от формата Markdown для ADR"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى وثائق MADR في الدليل `apps/docs/docs/decisions/`","محدود بمشاريع CellixJS","يعتمد على تنسيق Markdown لADR"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"07fc09384c84a905e7a4763e1e4ee802c925ee6237ac8bf6f8cf64ea9230ee44","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('hookvibe/hookcode/file-context-planning', 'community', 'hookvibe', 'hookcode', 'hookvibe/hookcode', 'file-context-planning', 3, 1, 65, '2026-02-27T14:57:39Z', '2026-02-28T01:37:20.872Z', '7aa52f1175155280b7fbd818b246a816c10db5ed130dc5a501a6e76a60eebc22', '{"id":"hookvibe/hookcode/file-context-planning","name":"file-context-planning","description":{"zh":"HookCode 支持独立部署，提供实时任务执行监控的可视化控制台","ja":"HookCode は独立したデプロイをサポートし、リアルタイムのタスク実行監視のための可視化コンソールを提供します","ko":"HookCode 는 독립적인 배포를 지원하며 실시간 작업 실행 모니터링을 위한 시각적 콘솔을 제공합니다","es":"HookCode es una plataforma de revisión y automatización de código inteligente que utiliza la planificación de contexto de archivo para desencadenar asistentes de codificación de CLI","fr":"HookCode est une plateforme d''examen et d''automatisation de code intelligente qui utilise la planification de contexte de fichier pour déclencher les assistants de codage de CLI","de":"HookCode ist eine intelligente Plattform für Code-Überprüfung und -Automatisierung, die die Datei-Kontext-Planung nutzt, um CLI-Coding-Assistenten auszulösen","pt":"HookCode é uma plataforma de revisão e automação de código que integra assistentes de codificação CLI e Webhooks para melhorar a produtividade","ru":"HookCode — это платформа для код-ревью и автоматизации, которая интегрирует CLI-кодирующие помощники и Webhooks для повышения производительности","ar":"HookCode هو منصة لمراجعة وتنفيذ الأوامر التلقائية التي تدمج مساعدي الترميز CLI والويب هوك لتحسين الإنتاجية","en":"HookCode is an intelligent code review and automation platform that elegantly triggers CLI coding assistants through conversations and Webhooks. It supports independent deployment and provides a visual console for real-time task execution monitoring."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代码审查工具 - file-context-planning","ja":"AIエージェントを使用したコードレビュー - file-context-planning","ko":"AI 에이전트를 활용한 코드 리뷰 - file-context-planning","es":"Herramientas de planificación de contexto de archivo con ...","fr":"Outils de planification de contexte de fichier avec les o...","de":"Datei-Kontext-Planung mit KI-Agents","pt":"Ferramentas de Planejamento de Contexto de Arquivo com Ag...","ru":"ИИ Агенты для Планирования Контекста Файлов","ar":"أدوات تخطيط سياق الملفات مع وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"file-context-planning"},"description":{"zh":"HookCode 支持独立部署，提供实时任务执行监控的可视化控制台","ja":"HookCode は独立したデプロイをサポートし、リアルタイムのタスク実行監視のための可視化コンソールを提供します","ko":"HookCode 는 독립적인 배포를 지원하며 실시간 작업 실행 모니터링을 위한 시각적 콘솔을 제공합니다","es":"HookCode es una plataforma de revisión y automatización de código inteligente que utiliza la planificación de contexto de archivo para desencadenar asistente...","fr":"HookCode est une plateforme d''examen et d''automatisation de code intelligente qui utilise la planification de contexte de fichier pour déclencher les assista...","de":"HookCode ist eine intelligente Plattform für Code-Überprüfung und -Automatisierung, die die Datei-Kontext-Planung nutzt, um CLI-Coding-Assistenten auszulösen","pt":"HookCode é uma plataforma de revisão e automação de código que integra assistentes de codificação CLI e Webhooks para melhorar a produtividade","ru":"HookCode — это платформа для код-ревью и автоматизации, которая интегрирует CLI-кодирующие помощники и Webhooks для повышения производительности","ar":"HookCode هو منصة لمراجعة وتنفيذ الأوامر التلقائية التي تدمج مساعدي الترميز CLI والويب هوك لتحسين الإنتاجية","en":"HookCode is an intelligent code review and automation platform that elegantly triggers CLI coding assistants through conversations and Webhooks. It supports ..."},"definition":{"en":"HookCode is an intelligent code review and automation platform that elegantly triggers CLI coding assistants through conversations and Webhooks. It supports independent deployment and provides a visual console for real-time task execution monitoring."},"features":{"zh":["支持通过对话和 Webhooks 触发 CLI 编码助手","独立部署支持","实时任务执行监控的可视化控制台","智能代码审查和自动化","支持多种编程语言"],"ja":["会話と Webhooks を介して CLI コーディング アシスタントをトリガーする機能","独立したデプロイのサポート","リアルタイムのタスク実行監視のための可視化コンソール","智能コード レビューと自動化","複数のプログラミング言語のサポート"],"ko":["대화와 Webhooks 를 통해 CLI 코딩 어시스턴트를 트리거하는 기능","독립적인 배포 지원","실시간 작업 실행 모니터링을 위한 시각적 콘솔","인텔리전트 코드 리뷰 및 자동화","다수의 프로그래밍 언어 지원"],"es":["Automatización de la revisión de código","Desencadenamiento de asistentes de codificación de CLI","Implementación independiente","Consola visual para el monitoreo de la ejecución de tareas en tiempo real"],"fr":["Automatisation de la révision de code","Déclenchement des assistants de codage de CLI","Déploiement indépendant","Console visuelle pour le suivi de l''exécution des tâches en temps réel"],"de":["Automatisierung der Code-Überprüfung","Auslösen von CLI-Coding-Assistenten","Unabhängige Bereitstellung","Visuelle Konsole für die Überwachung der Aufgabenausführung in Echtzeit"],"pt":["Integração com assistentes de codificação CLI","Suporte a Webhooks para automação","Console visual para monitoramento em tempo real","Desenvolvimento independente","Automatização de tarefas de codificação"],"ru":["Интеграция с CLI-кодировочными помощниками","Поддержка Webhooks для автоматизации","Визуальный консоль для мониторинга в реальном времени","Независимое развёртывание","Автоматизация задач кодирования"],"ar":["التكامل مع مساعدي الترميز CLI","دعم الويب هوك للتنفيذ التلقائي","واجهة مرئية لمراقبة الوقت الفعلي","التطوير المستقل","تنفيذ العمليات التلقائية للترميز"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代码审查","HookCode 介绍","代码审查工具","CLI 编码助手","如何使用 HookCode","HookCode 安装","代码自动化","代码审查平台","智能代码审查工具"],"ja":["AIエージェントを使用したコードレビュー","HookCode の概要","コードレビューツール","CLI コーディング アシスタント","HookCode の使い方","HookCode のインストール","コード自動化","コードレビュー プラットフォーム","智能コード レビュー ツール"],"ko":["AI 에이전트를 활용한 코드 리뷰","HookCode 소개","코드 리뷰 도구","CLI 코딩 어시스턴트","HookCode 사용 방법","HookCode 설치","코드 자동화","코드 리뷰 플랫폼","인텔리전트 코드 리뷰 도구"],"es":["cómo utilizar HookCode","qué es la planificación de contexto de archivo","alternativas a HookCode","HookCode vs otros herramientas de revisión de código","instalación de HookCode","guía de configuración de HookCode"],"fr":["comment utiliser HookCode","quoi est la planification de contexte de fichier","alternatives à HookCode","HookCode vs autres outils d''examen de code","installation de HookCode","guide de configuration de HookCode"],"de":["wie man HookCode verwendet","was ist die Datei-Kontext-Planung","Alternativen zu HookCode","HookCode vs andere Code-Überprüfungstools","Installation von HookCode","Einrichtungsanleitung für HookCode"],"pt":["como usar HookCode","o que é planejamento de contexto de arquivo","ferramentas de automação de código","alternativas para HookCode","HookCode vs outros","instalar HookCode","guia de configuração do HookCode"],"ru":["как использовать HookCode","что такое планирование контекста файла","инструменты автоматизации кода","альтернативы для HookCode","HookCode vs другие","установить HookCode","руководство по настройке HookCode"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام HookCode","ما هو تخطيط سياق الملف","أدوات تنفيذ الأوامر التلقائية للترميز","بديل ل HookCode","HookCode مقابل غيره","تثبيت HookCode","دليل إعداد HookCode"]}},"owner":"hookvibe","repo":"hookcode","repoPath":"hookvibe/hookcode","stars":3,"forks":1,"updatedAt":"2026-02-27T14:57:39Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"file-context-planning","description":"Manus-style file-based planning for Codex CLI. Stores task_plan.md/findings.md/progress.md under docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>/ for durable planning + traceability.","version":"4.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Planning with Files (Codex)\n\n<!-- Align this Claude skill''s path examples with the .claude directory layout. docs/en/developer/plans/claude-skills-audit-20260227/task_plan.md claude-skills-audit-20260227 -->\nWork like Manus: Use persistent markdown files as your \"working memory on disk.\"\n{/* Refactor planning files to live under docs/en/developer/plans/<hash> for traceability. sddsa89612jk4hbwas678 */}\n\n## What This Skill Does (Codex-Compatible)\n\nCodex skills are instruction-only. There are **","body":"# Planning with Files (Codex)\n\n<!-- Align this Claude skill''s path examples with the .claude directory layout. docs/en/developer/plans/claude-skills-audit-20260227/task_plan.md claude-skills-audit-20260227 -->\nWork like Manus: Use persistent markdown files as your \"working memory on disk.\"\n{/* Refactor planning files to live under docs/en/developer/plans/<hash> for traceability. sddsa89612jk4hbwas678 */}\n\n## What This Skill Does (Codex-Compatible)\n\nCodex skills are instruction-only. There are **no automatic hooks** (e.g., \"PreToolUse\", \"Stop\").\n\nTo get the benefits, you must **manually**:\n- Create a **session folder** under `docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>/`\n- Re-read `task_plan.md` before major decisions\n- Update `task_plan.md`, `findings.md`, and `progress.md` throughout the work\n- Add the same `<session-hash>` into inline code comments for traceability\n\n## Operational Checklist (Replace Claude Hooks)\n\nWhen using this skill on a complex task:\n\n1. Create a new session hash (example: `sddsa89612jk4hbwas678`).\n2. If `docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>/` does not exist, initialize it (script or template copy).\n3. Fill `task_plan.md` (goal, phases, key questions) **before** implementing anything.\n4. Before major decisions or phase changes, re-read `task_plan.md` (refreshes goals into the attention window).\n5. After every 2 information-gathering actions, append key discoveries into `findings.md` (2-Action Rule).\n6. After completing a phase, return to the session folder and update:\n   - phase status in `task_plan.md`\n   - session log + tests in `progress.md`\n7. When the task is done, update `docs/en/change-log/0.0.0.md` with the hash + one-line summary + relative link to the plan.\n\n## Important: Where Files Go (Repo Layout)\n\nWhen using this skill:\n\n- **Skill assets** (templates/scripts/reference) live in: `.claude/skills/file-context-planning/`\n  - Templates: `.claude/skills/file-context-planning/templates/`\n  - Scripts: `.claude/skills/file-context-planning/scripts/`\n- **Your planning files** live in a **hash folder** under: `docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>/`\n\n| Location | What Goes There |\n|----------|-----------------|\n| Skill directory (`.claude/skills/file-context-planning/`) | Templates, scripts, reference docs |\n| `docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>/` | `task_plan.md`, `findings.md`, `progress.md` |\n\nThis ensures your planning files are:\n- durable (versionable docs)\n- easy to link to (relative links)\n- traceable from code via the session hash\n\n## Quick Start\n\nBefore ANY complex task:\n\n### Option A: Initialize via Script (Fastest)\n\nCreates `docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>/` and copies templates there if missing.\n{/* Document docs navigation sync behavior (Mintlify vs Docusaurus). docs/en/developer/plans/dsim8xybp9oa18nz1gfq/task_plan.md dsim8xybp9oa18nz1gfq */}\nAlso syncs `docs/docs.json` when present (Mintlify) so the new session files are discoverable; if `docs/docs.json` is absent (Docusaurus), the sync step is skipped.\n\n```bash\nbash .claude/skills/file-context-planning/scripts/init-session.sh \"<session-hash>\" \"<session-title>\"\n```\n\nIf you need a one-off backfill or want to rebuild the navigation index deterministically:\n\n```bash\nbash .claude/skills/file-context-planning/scripts/sync-docs-json-plans.sh\n```\n\n### Option B: Copy Templates (Most Detailed)\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>\ncp .claude/skills/file-context-planning/templates/task_plan.md docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>/task_plan.md\ncp .claude/skills/file-context-planning/templates/findings.md docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>/findings.md\ncp .claude/skills/file-context-planning/templates/progress.md docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>/progress.md\n```\n\nThen:\n\n1. **Fill `task_plan.md` first** — Goal, phases, key questions\n2. **Re-read plan before decisions** — Refreshes goals in the attention window\n3. **Update after each phase** — Mark status complete, log errors\n4. **Log discoveries continuously** — `findings.md` for knowledge, `progress.md` for session/test logs\n\nOptional completion check:\n\n```bash\nbash .claude/skills/file-context-planning/scripts/check-complete.sh <session-hash>\n```\n\n> **Note:** All three planning files should be created in `docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>/`, not in your project root and not in the skill folder.\n\n## The Core Pattern\n\n```\nContext Window = RAM (volatile, limited)\nFilesystem = Disk (persistent, unlimited)\n\n→ Anything important gets written to disk.\n```\n\n## File Purposes\n\n| File | Purpose | When to Update |\n|------|---------|----------------|\n| `task_plan.md` | Phases, progress, decisions | After each phase |\n| `findings.md` | Research, discoveries | After ANY discovery |\n| `progress.md` | Session log, test results | Throughout session |\n\n## Traceability: Hash in Inline Comments\n\nTo link code changes back to the plan folder, include the session hash in **every changed area** via an inline comment:\n\n{/* Align traceability format with repo-root AGENTS.md (include plan path + hash). docs/en/developer/plans/docsworkflowapi20260121/task_plan.md docsworkflowapi20260121 */}\n**Format:** `<one sentence in English> <relative-plan-path> <session-hash>`\n\n**Plan path:** `docs/en/developer/plans/<session-hash>/task_plan.md`\n\nExamples:\n\n- JS/TS/Go: `// Add input validation for webhook payload. docs/en/developer/plans/sddsa89612jk4hbwas678/task_plan.md sddsa89612jk4hbwas678`\n- Python/Shell/YAML: `# Document retry backoff behavior. docs/en/developer/plans/sddsa89612jk4hbwas678/task_plan.md sddsa89612jk4hbwas678`\n- SQL: `-- Prevent duplicate inserts via unique key. docs/en/developer/plans/sddsa89612jk4hbwas678/task_plan.md sddsa89612jk4hbwas678`\n- Markdown: `{/* Explain why this doc section changed. docs/en/developer/plans/sddsa89612jk4hbwas678/task_plan.md sddsa89612jk4hbwas678 */}`\n\nThis creates a stable backlink: comment → hash → `docs/en/developer/plans/<hash>/`.\n\n## Release Note Update (Required)\n\nWhen the task is completed, update `docs/en/change-log/0.0.0.md` with:\n- the session hash\n- a one-line summary\n- a relative link to the plan (recommend linking `task_plan.md`)\n\nExample entry:\n\n```md\n- sddsa89612jk4hbwas678: Refactor file-context-planning to store plans in hash folders. ([plan](../developer/plans/sddsa89612jk4hbwas678/task_plan.md))\n```\n\n{/* Keep changelog entries clean and single-line (no extra HTML comment lines). l290bb7v758opd6uxu6r */}\n> **Note:** Do not add an extra `{/* ... */}` line above changelog bullets. The bullet itself (hash + plan link) is enough traceability.\n\n{/* Prefer stdin to avoid shell expansion when summaries contain code-like characters. l290bb7v758opd6uxu6r */}\n> **Tip:** If your summary contains backticks or other shell-sensitive characters, pipe it via stdin: `printf ''%s'' \"<summary>\" | bash .claude/skills/file-context-planning/scripts/append-changelog.sh \"<hash>\"`.\n\n## Critical Rules\n\n### 1. Create Plan First\nNever start a complex task without a session folder containing `task_plan.md`. Non-negotiable.\n\n### 2. The 2-Action Rule\n> \"After every 2 information-gathering actions, IMMEDIATELY save key findings to text files.\"\n\nThis prevents visual/multimodal information from being lost.\n\n### 3. Read Before Decide\nBefore major decisions, read the plan file. This keeps goals in your attention window.\n\n### 4. Update After Act\nAfter completing any phase:\n- Mark phase status: `in_progress` → `complete`\n- Log any errors encountered\n- Note files created/modified\n\n### 5. Log ALL Errors\nEvery error goes in the plan file. This builds knowledge and prevents repetition.\n\n```markdown\n## Errors Encountered\n| Error | Attempt | Resolution |\n|-------|---------|------------|\n| FileNotFoundError | 1 | Created default config |\n| API timeout | 2 | Added retry logic |\n```\n\n### 6. Never Repeat Failures\n```\nif action_failed:\n    next_action != same_action\n```\nTrack what you tried. Mutate the approach.\n\n## The 3-Strike Error Protocol\n\n```\nATTEMPT 1: Diagnose & Fix\n  → Read error carefully\n  → Identify root cause\n  → Apply targeted fix\n\nATTEMPT 2: Alternative Approach\n  → Same error? Try different method\n  → Different tool? Different library?\n  → NEVER repeat exact same failing action\n\nATTEMPT 3: Broader Rethink\n  → Question assumptions\n  → Search for solutions\n  → Consider updating the plan\n\nAFTER 3 FAILURES: Escalate to User\n  → Explain what you tried\n  → Share the specific error\n  → Ask for guidance\n```\n\n## Read vs Write Decision Matrix\n\n| Situation | Action | Reason |\n|-----------|--------|--------|\n| Just wrote a file | DON''T read | Content still in context |\n| Viewed image/PDF | Write findings NOW | Multimodal → text before lost |\n| Browser returned data | Write to file | Screenshots don''t persist |\n| Starting new phase | Read plan/findings | Re-orient if context stale |\n| Error occurred | Read relevant file | Need current state to fix |\n| Resuming after gap | Read all planning files | Recover state |\n\n## The 5-Question Reboot Test\n\nIf you can answer these, your context management is solid:\n\n| Question | Answer Source |\n|----------|---------------|\n| Where am I? | Current phase in task_plan.md |\n| Where am I going? | Remaining phases |\n| What''s the goal? | Goal statement in plan |\n| What have I learned? | findings.md |\n| What have I done? | progress.md |\n\n## When to Use This Pattern\n\n**Use for:**\n- Multi-step tasks (3+ steps)\n- Research tasks\n- Building/creating projects\n- Tasks spanning many tool calls\n- Anything requiring organization\n\n**Skip for:**\n- Simple questions\n- Single-file edits\n- Quick lookups\n\n## Templates\n\nCopy these templates to start:\n\n- [templates/task_plan.md](templates/task_plan.md) — Phase tracking\n- [templates/findings.md](templates/findings.md) — Research storage\n- [templates/progress.md](templates/progress.md) — Session logging\n\n## Scripts\n\nHelper scripts for automation:\n\n- `scripts/init-session.sh` — Initialize all planning files\n- `scripts/check-complete.sh` — Verify all phases complete\n- `scripts/append-changelog.sh` — Append changelog entry (hash + plan link)\n\n## Advanced Topics\n\n- **Manus Principles:** See [reference.md](reference.md)\n- **Real Examples:** See [examples.md](examples.md)\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Don''t | Do Instead |\n|-------|------------|\n| Keep todos only in chat memory | Persist the plan in task_plan.md |\n| State goals once and forget | Re-read plan before decisions |\n| Hide errors and retry silently | Log errors to plan file |\n| Stuff everything in context | Store large content in files |\n| Start executing immediately | Create plan file FIRST |\n| Repeat failed actions | Track attempts, mutate approach |\n| Create planning files in repo root | Create `docs/en/developer/plans/<hash>/` |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-28T01:37:20.872Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review and Automation Agents needing persistent file-based context management.","zh":"非常适合需要基于文件的持久化上下文管理的代码审查和自动化Agent。","ja":"ファイルベースの永続的なコンテキスト管理を必要とするコードレビューおよび自動化エージェントに最適です。","ko":"파일 기반의 지속적인 컨텍스트 관리가 필요한 코드 리뷰 및 자동화 에이전트에 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código y automatización que necesitan gestión de contexto persistente basada en archivos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de revue de code et d''automatisation nécessitant une gestion de contexte persistante basée sur des fichiers.","de":"Perfekt für Code Review und Automation Agents, die eine persistente dateibasierte Kontextverwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código e Automação que necessitam de gestão de contexto persistente baseada em ficheiros.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Агентов проверки кода и автоматизации, которым требуется управление контекстом на основе постоянных файлов.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء مراجعة التعليمات البرمجية والأتمتة التي تحتاج إلى إدارة سياق مستدامة قائمة على الملفات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to maintain working memory on disk through persistent markdown files, supporting independent deployment and real-time task execution monitoring via visual console. Integrates seamlessly with CLI coding assistants through conversation triggers and Webhooks.","zh":"使Agent能够通过持久化的markdown文件在磁盘上维护工作内存，支持独立部署并通过可视化控制台实时监控任务执行。通过对话触发器和Webhooks与CLI编码助手无缝集成。","ja":"エージェントが永続的なmarkdownファイルを通じてディスク上で作業メモリを維持できるようにし、独立したデプロイとビジュアルコンソールによるリアルタイムタスク実行の監視をサポートします。会話トリガーとWebhooksを通じてCLIコーディングアシスタントとシームレスに統合します。","ko":"에이전트가 지속적인 markdown 파일을 통해 디스크에 작업 메모리를 유지할 수 있도록 하여, 독립적인 배포와 시각적 콘솔을 통한 실시간 작업 실행 모니터링을 지원합니다. 대화 트리거와 Webhooks를 통해 CLI 코딩 어시스턴트와 원활하게 통합됩니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes mantener la memoria de trabajo en disco mediante archivos markdown persistentes, soportando despliegue independiente y monitorización de ejecución de tareas en tiempo real mediante consola visual. Se integra perfectamente con asistentes de codificación CLI a través de disparadores de conversación y Webhooks.","fr":"Permet aux agents de maintenir une mémoire de travail sur disque via des fichiers markdown persistants, supportant un déploiement indépendant et une surveillance de l''exécution des tâches en temps réel via une console visuelle. S''intègre parfaitement avec les assistants de codification CLI via des déclencheurs de conversation et des Webhooks.","de":"Ermöglicht Agents, Arbeitsspeicher auf der Festplatte durch persistente Markdown-Dateien zu verwalten, unterstützt unabhängiges Deployment und Echtzeit-Überwachung der Aufgabenausführung via visueller Konsole. Integriert sich nahtlos mit CLI Coding Assistants durch Konversationstrigger und Webhooks.","pt":"Permite que os agentes mantenham a memória de trabalho em disco através de ficheiros markdown persistentes, suportando implementação independente e monitorização em tempo real da execução de tarefas através de consola visual. Integra-se perfeitamente com assistentes de codificação CLI através de triggers de conversação e Webhooks.","ru":"Позволяет агентам сохранять рабочую память на диске через постоянные файлы markdown, поддерживая независимое развертывание и мониторинг выполнения задач в реальном времени через визуальную консоль. Легко интегрируется с CLI-ассистентами кодирования через триггеры беседы и Webhooks.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من الحفاظ على الذاكرة العاملة على القرص من خلال ملفات markdown مستدامة، مما يدعم النشر المستقل ومراقبة تنفيذ المهام في الوقت الفعلي عبر وحدة تحكم بصرية. يتكامل بسلاسة مع مساعدي الترميز CLI من خلال محفزات المحادثة وWebhooks."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code review workflows via Webhook triggers","Monitoring real-time task execution through visual console","Maintaining persistent planning context in markdown files","Triggering CLI assistants through conversational interfaces"],"zh":["通过Webhook触发器自动化代码审查工作流程","通过可视化控制台监控实时任务执行","在markdown文件中维护持久的规划上下文","通过对话界面触发CLI助手"],"ja":["Webhookトリガーによるコードレビューワークフローの自動化","ビジュアルコンソールによるリアルタイムタスク実行の監視","markdownファイル内での永続的な計画コンテキストの維持","会話インターフェースを通じたCLIアシスタントのトリガー"],"ko":["Webhook 트리거를 통한 코드 리뷰 워크플로우 자동화","시각적 콘솔을 통한 실시간 작업 실행 모니터링","markdown 파일에서 지속적인 계획 컨텍스트 유지","대화형 인터페이스를 통한 CLI 어시스턴트 트리거"],"es":["Automatización de flujos de trabajo de revisión de código mediante disparadores Webhook","Monitorización de ejecución de tareas en tiempo real mediante consola visual","Mantenimiento de contexto de planificación persistente en archivos markdown","Disparar asistentes CLI mediante interfaces conversacionales"],"fr":["Automatisation des flux de travail de revue de code via des déclencheurs Webhook","Surveillance de l''exécution des tâches en temps réel via une console visuelle","Maintien d''un contexte de planification persistant dans des fichiers markdown","Déclenchement d''assistants CLI via des interfaces conversationnelles"],"de":["Automatisierung von Code Review Workflows via Webhook-Triggern","Überwachung der Echtzeit-Aufgabenausführung durch visuelle Konsole","Aufrechterhaltung eines persistenten Planungskontextes in Markdown-Dateien","Auslösen von CLI-Assistenten durch konversationelle Schnittstellen"],"pt":["Automatização de fluxos de trabalho de revisão de código através de triggers de Webhook","Monitorização da execução de tarefas em tempo real através de consola visual","Manutenção de contexto de planeamento persistente em ficheiros markdown","Ativação de assistentes CLI através de interfaces conversacionais"],"ru":["Автоматизация рабочих процессов проверки кода через триггеры Webhook","Мониторинг выполнения задач в реальном времени через визуальную консоль","Поддержание постоянного контекста планирования в файлах markdown","Активация CLI-ассистентов через разговорные интерфейсы"],"ar":["أتمتة سير عمل مراجعة التعليمات البرمجية عبر محفزات Webhook","مراقبة تنفيذ المهام في الوقت الفعلي عبر وحدة تحكم بصرية","الحفاظ على سياق التخطيط المستدام في ملفات markdown","تشغيل مساعدي CLI عبر واجهات المحادثة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires filesystem access for markdown persistence","Needs Webhook configuration for automation","Depends on .claude directory structure compatibility"],"zh":["需要文件系统访问权限以实现markdown持久化","需要Webhook配置以实现自动化","依赖.claude目录结构的兼容性"],"ja":["markdownの永続化にはファイルシステムアクセスが必要","自動化にはWebhookの設定が必要",".claudeディレクトリ構造の互換性に依存"],"ko":["markdown 지속성을 위한 파일 시스템 액세스 필요","자동화를 위한 Webhook 구성 필요",".claude 디렉토리 구조 호환성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso al sistema de archivos para la persistencia de markdown","Necesita configuración de Webhook para la automatización","Depende de la compatibilidad con la estructura de directorio .claude"],"fr":["Requiert un accès au système de fichiers pour la persistance markdown","Nécessite une configuration Webhook pour l''automatisation","Dépend de la compatibilité avec la structure de répertoire .claude"],"de":["Erfordert Dateisystemzugriff für Markdown-Persistenz","Benötigt Webhook-Konfiguration für die Automatisierung","Ist abhängig von der Kompatibilität der .claude-Verzeichnisstruktur"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao sistema de ficheiros para persistência de markdown","Necessita de configuração de Webhook para automação","Depende da compatibilidade da estrutura de diretório .claude"],"ru":["Требует доступ к файловой системе для сохранения markdown","Требует настройки Webhook для автоматизации","Зависит от совместимости структуры каталога .claude"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى نظام الملفات لاستدامة markdown","يحتاج إلى تكوين Webhook للأتمتة","يعتمد على توافق بنية دليل .claude"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"7aa52f1175155280b7fbd818b246a816c10db5ed130dc5a501a6e76a60eebc22","qualityScore":65}');
