component-authoring","alternativas para criação de componentes","convex-component-authoring vs outros","instalar convex-component-authoring","guia de configuração para desenvolvedores","desenvolvimento de componentes com IA","ferramentas de desenvolvimento de componentes","tecnologia de ponta para desenvolvedores"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое Convex-component-authoring","альтернативы для создания компонентов","Convex-component-authoring vs другие","установить Convex-component-authoring","руководство по настройке для разработчиков","разработка компонентов с помощью ИИ","инструменты разработки компонентов","перспективные технологии для разработчиков"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هي تقنية إنشاء المكونات المتقاربة","بديلات لإنشاء المكونات","تقنية إنشاء المكونات المتقاربة مقابل الأخرى","تثبيت تقنية إنشاء المكونات المتقاربة","دليل الإعداد للمطورين","تطوير المكونات باستخدام الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات تطوير المكونات","تقنيات متقدمة للمطورين"]}},"owner":"kimmyxpow","repo":"recallable","repoPath":"kimmyxpow/recallable","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T12:47:24.668Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"convex-component-authoring","description":"How to create, structure, and publish self-contained Convex components with proper isolation, exports, and dependency management","version":"1.0.0","tags":["convex","components","reusable","packages","npm"],"bodyPreview":"# Convex Component Authoring\n\nCreate self-contained, reusable Convex components with proper isolation, exports, and dependency management for sharing across projects.\n\n## Documentation Sources\n\nBefore implementing, do not assume; fetch the latest documentation:\n\n- Primary: https://docs.convex.dev/components\n- Component Authoring: https://docs.convex.dev/components/authoring\n- For broader context: https://docs.convex.dev/llms.txt\n\n## Instructions\n\n### What Are Convex Components?\n\nConvex component","body":"# Convex Component Authoring\n\nCreate self-contained, reusable Convex components with proper isolation, exports, and dependency management for sharing across projects.\n\n## Documentation Sources\n\nBefore implementing, do not assume; fetch the latest documentation:\n\n- Primary: https://docs.convex.dev/components\n- Component Authoring: https://docs.convex.dev/components/authoring\n- For broader context: https://docs.convex.dev/llms.txt\n\n## Instructions\n\n### What Are Convex Components?\n\nConvex components are self-contained packages that include:\n- Database tables (isolated from the main app)\n- Functions (queries, mutations, actions)\n- TypeScript types and validators\n- Optional frontend hooks\n\n### Component Structure\n\n```\nmy-convex-component/\n├── package.json\n├── tsconfig.json\n├── README.md\n├── src/\n│   ├── index.ts           # Main exports\n│   ├── component.ts       # Component definition\n│   ├── schema.ts          # Component schema\n│   └── functions/\n│       ├── queries.ts\n│       ├── mutations.ts\n│       └── actions.ts\n└── convex.config.ts       # Component configuration\n```\n\n### Creating a Component\n\n#### 1. Component Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// convex.config.ts\nimport { defineComponent } from \"convex/server\";\n\nexport default defineComponent(\"myComponent\");\n```\n\n#### 2. Component Schema\n\n```typescript\n// src/schema.ts\nimport { defineSchema, defineTable } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport default defineSchema({\n  // Tables are isolated to this component\n  items: defineTable({\n    name: v.string(),\n    data: v.any(),\n    createdAt: v.number(),\n  }).index(\"by_name\", [\"name\"]),\n  \n  config: defineTable({\n    key: v.string(),\n    value: v.any(),\n  }).index(\"by_key\", [\"key\"]),\n});\n```\n\n#### 3. Component Definition\n\n```typescript\n// src/component.ts\nimport { defineComponent, ComponentDefinition } from \"convex/server\";\nimport schema from \"./schema\";\nimport * as queries from \"./functions/queries\";\nimport * as mutations from \"./functions/mutations\";\n\nconst component = defineComponent(\"myComponent\", {\n  schema,\n  functions: {\n    ...queries,\n    ...mutations,\n  },\n});\n\nexport default component;\n```\n\n#### 4. Component Functions\n\n```typescript\n// src/functions/queries.ts\nimport { query } from \"../_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport const list = query({\n  args: {\n    limit: v.optional(v.number()),\n  },\n  returns: v.array(v.object({\n    _id: v.id(\"items\"),\n    name: v.string(),\n    data: v.any(),\n    createdAt: v.number(),\n  })),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    return await ctx.db\n      .query(\"items\")\n      .order(\"desc\")\n      .take(args.limit ?? 10);\n  },\n});\n\nexport const get = query({\n  args: { name: v.string() },\n  returns: v.union(v.object({\n    _id: v.id(\"items\"),\n    name: v.string(),\n    data: v.any(),\n  }), v.null()),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    return await ctx.db\n      .query(\"items\")\n      .withIndex(\"by_name\", (q) => q.eq(\"name\", args.name))\n      .unique();\n  },\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// src/functions/mutations.ts\nimport { mutation } from \"../_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport const create = mutation({\n  args: {\n    name: v.string(),\n    data: v.any(),\n  },\n  returns: v.id(\"items\"),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    return await ctx.db.insert(\"items\", {\n      name: args.name,\n      data: args.data,\n      createdAt: Date.now(),\n    });\n  },\n});\n\nexport const update = mutation({\n  args: {\n    id: v.id(\"items\"),\n    data: v.any(),\n  },\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    await ctx.db.patch(args.id, { data: args.data });\n    return null;\n  },\n});\n\nexport const remove = mutation({\n  args: { id: v.id(\"items\") },\n  returns: v.null(),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    await ctx.db.delete(args.id);\n    return null;\n  },\n});\n```\n\n#### 5. Main Exports\n\n```typescript\n// src/index.ts\nexport { default as component } from \"./component\";\nexport * from \"./functions/queries\";\nexport * from \"./functions/mutations\";\n\n// Export types for consumers\nexport type { Id } from \"./_generated/dataModel\";\n```\n\n### Using a Component\n\n```typescript\n// In the consuming app''s convex/convex.config.ts\nimport { defineApp } from \"convex/server\";\nimport myComponent from \"my-convex-component\";\n\nconst app = defineApp();\n\napp.use(myComponent, { name: \"myComponent\" });\n\nexport default app;\n```\n\n```typescript\n// In the consuming app''s code\nimport { useQuery, useMutation } from \"convex/react\";\nimport { api } from \"../convex/_generated/api\";\n\nfunction MyApp() {\n  // Access component functions through the app''s API\n  const items = useQuery(api.myComponent.list, { limit: 10 });\n  const createItem = useMutation(api.myComponent.create);\n  \n  return (\n    <div>\n      {items?.map((item) => (\n        <div key={item._id}>{item.name}</div>\n      ))}\n      <button onClick={() => createItem({ name: \"New\", data: {} })}>\n        Add Item\n      </button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Component Configuration Options\n\n```typescript\n// convex/convex.config.ts\nimport { defineApp } from \"convex/server\";\nimport myComponent from \"my-convex-component\";\n\nconst app = defineApp();\n\n// Basic usage\napp.use(myComponent);\n\n// With custom name\napp.use(myComponent, { name: \"customName\" });\n\n// Multiple instances\napp.use(myComponent, { name: \"instance1\" });\napp.use(myComponent, { name: \"instance2\" });\n\nexport default app;\n```\n\n### Providing Component Hooks\n\n```typescript\n// src/hooks.ts\nimport { useQuery, useMutation } from \"convex/react\";\nimport { FunctionReference } from \"convex/server\";\n\n// Type-safe hooks for component consumers\nexport function useMyComponent(api: {\n  list: FunctionReference<\"query\">;\n  create: FunctionReference<\"mutation\">;\n}) {\n  const items = useQuery(api.list, {});\n  const createItem = useMutation(api.create);\n  \n  return {\n    items,\n    createItem,\n    isLoading: items === undefined,\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### Publishing a Component\n\n#### package.json\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-convex-component\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"description\": \"A reusable Convex component\",\n  \"main\": \"dist/index.js\",\n  \"types\": \"dist/index.d.ts\",\n  \"files\": [\n    \"dist\",\n    \"convex.config.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsc\",\n    \"prepublishOnly\": \"npm run build\"\n  },\n  \"peerDependencies\": {\n    \"convex\": \"^1.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"convex\": \"^1.17.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"convex\",\n    \"component\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n#### tsconfig.json\n\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2020\",\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"declaration\": true,\n    \"outDir\": \"dist\",\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src/**/*\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"node_modules\", \"dist\"]\n}\n```\n\n## Examples\n\n### Rate Limiter Component\n\n```typescript\n// rate-limiter/src/schema.ts\nimport { defineSchema, defineTable } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport default defineSchema({\n  requests: defineTable({\n    key: v.string(),\n    timestamp: v.number(),\n  })\n    .index(\"by_key\", [\"key\"])\n    .index(\"by_key_and_time\", [\"key\", \"timestamp\"]),\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// rate-limiter/src/functions/mutations.ts\nimport { mutation } from \"../_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport const checkLimit = mutation({\n  args: {\n    key: v.string(),\n    limit: v.number(),\n    windowMs: v.number(),\n  },\n  returns: v.object({\n    allowed: v.boolean(),\n    remaining: v.number(),\n    resetAt: v.number(),\n  }),\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const now = Date.now();\n    const windowStart = now - args.windowMs;\n    \n    // Clean old entries\n    const oldEntries = await ctx.db\n      .query(\"requests\")\n      .withIndex(\"by_key_and_time\", (q) => \n        q.eq(\"key\", args.key).lt(\"timestamp\", windowStart)\n      )\n      .collect();\n    \n    for (const entry of oldEntries) {\n      await ctx.db.delete(entry._id);\n    }\n    \n    // Count current window\n    const currentRequests = await ctx.db\n      .query(\"requests\")\n      .withIndex(\"by_key\", (q) => q.eq(\"key\", args.key))\n      .collect();\n    \n    const remaining = Math.max(0, args.limit - currentRequests.length);\n    const allowed = remaining > 0;\n    \n    if (allowed) {\n      await ctx.db.insert(\"requests\", {\n        key: args.key,\n        timestamp: now,\n      });\n    }\n    \n    const oldestRequest = currentRequests[0];\n    const resetAt = oldestRequest \n      ? oldestRequest.timestamp + args.windowMs \n      : now + args.windowMs;\n    \n    return { allowed, remaining: remaining - (allowed ? 1 : 0), resetAt };\n  },\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Usage in consuming app\nimport { useMutation } from \"convex/react\";\nimport { api } from \"../convex/_generated/api\";\n\nfunction useRateLimitedAction() {\n  const checkLimit = useMutation(api.rateLimiter.checkLimit);\n  \n  return async (action: () => Promise<void>) => {\n    const result = await checkLimit({\n      key: \"user-action\",\n      limit: 10,\n      windowMs: 60000,\n    });\n    \n    if (!result.allowed) {\n      throw new Error(`Rate limited. Try again at ${new Date(result.resetAt)}`);\n    }\n    \n    await action();\n  };\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- Never run `npx convex deploy` unless explicitly instructed\n- Never run any git commands unless explicitly instructed\n- Keep component tables isolated (don''t reference main app tables)\n- Export clear TypeScript types for consumers\n- Document all public functions and their arguments\n- Use semantic versioning for component releases\n- Include comprehensive README with examples\n- Test components in isolation before publishing\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n1. **Cross-referencing tables** - Component tables should be self-contained\n2. **Missing type exports** - Export all necessary types\n3. **Hardcoded configuration** - Use component options for customization\n4. **No versioning** - Follow semantic versioning\n5. **Poor documentation** - Document all public APIs\n\n## References\n\n- Convex Documentation: https://docs.convex.dev/\n- Convex LLMs.txt: https://docs.convex.dev/llms.txt\n- Components: https://docs.convex.dev/components\n- Component Authoring: https://docs.convex.dev/components/authoring\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-01T13:22:11.362Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing reusable and isolated Convex component authoring capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要可重用和隔离Convex组件创建能力的全栈代理。","ja":"再利用可能で隔離されたConvexコンポーネントの作成機能が必要なフルスタックエージェントに最適です。","ko":"재사용 가능하고 분리된 Convex 컴포넌트 작성 기능이 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Full Stack que necesitan capacidades de autoría de componentes Convex reutilizables y aisladas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack ayant besoin de capacités de création de composants Convex réutilisables et isolées.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die wiederverwendbare und isolierte Convex-Komponenten-Autorisierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que precisam de capacidades de autorização de componentes Convex reutilizáveis e isoladas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Full Stack, которым необходимы функции создания многократно используемых и изолированных компонентов Convex.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الويب الكامل الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات كتابة مكونات Convex قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام ومفصولة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create self-contained Convex components with proper isolation, exports, and dependency management using the Convex documentation and API, enabling seamless sharing across projects and facilitating efficient collaboration through well-documented components.","zh":"赋予代理创建具有适当隔离、导出和依赖管理的自包含Convex组件的能力，使用Convex文档和API，实现跨项目的无缝共享，并通过文档齐全的组件促进高效的协作。","ja":"Convexの文書とAPIを使用して、適切な分離、エクスポート、および依存関係管理を備えたセルフコンテイナConvexコンポーネントを作成するエージェントを可能にし、プロジェクト間のシームレスな共有を実現し、文書化されたコンポーネントを通じて効率的なコラボレーションを促進します。","ko":"Convex 문서와 API를 사용하여 적절한 격리, 내보내기 및 종속성 관리를 갖춘 자체 포함 Convex 컴포넌트를 생성할 수 있는 에이전트를 가능하게 하여 프로젝트 간의 무힌공유를 가능하게 하고 문서화된 컴포넌트를 통해 효율적인 협력을 촉진합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear componentes Convex autocontenidos con un aislamiento adecuado, exportaciones y gestión de dependencias utilizando la documentación y la API de Convex, lo que permite una compartición fluida entre proyectos y facilita una colaboración eficiente a través de componentes bien documentados.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des composants Convex autocontenus avec un isolement approprié, des exportations et une gestion des dépendances en utilisant la documentation et l''API Convex, ce qui permet un partage fluide entre les projets et facilite une collaboration efficace grâce à des composants bien documentés.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, selbstenthaltene Convex-Komponenten mit ordnungsgemäßer Isolation, Exporten und Abhängigkeitsverwaltung unter Verwendung der Convex-Dokumentation und -API zu erstellen, was eine nahtlose Weitergabe zwischen Projekten ermöglicht und eine effiziente Zusammenarbeit durch gut dokumentierte Komponenten erleichtert.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem componentes Convex autocontidos com isolamento adequado, exportações e gerenciamento de dependências usando a documentação e a API do Convex, permitindo uma partilha sem problemas entre projetos e facilitando a colaboração eficiente por meio de componentes bem documentados.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать самодостаточные компоненты Convex с правильным изоляцией, экспортами и управлением зависимостями, используя документацию и API Convex, что позволяет легко делиться между проектами и облегчает эффективное сотрудничество за счет хорошо документированных компонентов.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء مكونات Convex مكتفية ذاتيا مع عزل مناسب وتصدير وإدارة التبعيات باستخدام وثائق وAPI Convex، مما يسمح بمشاركة بدون مشاكل عبر المشاريع ويتيسر التعاون الفعال من خلال مكونات وثائقها جيدا."},"useCases":{"en":["Authoring reusable Convex components for cross-project sharing","Implementing dependency management for Convex components","Exporting Convex components for integration into larger applications"],"zh":["为跨项目共享编写可重用Convex组件","为Convex组件实现依赖管理","将Convex组件导出以集成到更大的应用程序中"],"ja":["プロジェクト間で共有するための再利用可能なConvexコンポーネントの作成","Convexコンポーネントの依存関係管理の実装","より大きなアプリケーションに統合するためのConvexコンポーネントのエクスポート"],"ko":["프로젝트 간 공유를 위한 재사용 가능한 Convex 컴포넌트 작성","Convex 컴포넌트에 대한 종속성 관리 구현","더 큰 애플리케이션에 통합하기 위한 Convex 컴포넌트 내보내기"],"es":["Creación de componentes Convex reutilizables para compartir entre proyectos","Implementación de la gestión de dependencias para componentes Convex","Exportación de componentes Convex para integrarlos en aplicaciones más grandes"],"fr":["Création de composants Convex réutilisables pour un partage entre les projets","Mise en œuvre de la gestion des dépendances pour les composants Convex","Exportation de composants Convex pour les intégrer dans des applications plus grandes"],"de":["Erstellung wiederverwendbarer Convex-Komponenten zur Weitergabe zwischen Projekten","Implementierung der Abhängigkeitsverwaltung für Convex-Komponenten","Export von Convex-Komponenten zur Integration in größere Anwendungen"],"pt":["Criação de componentes Convex reutilizáveis para partilha entre projetos","Implementação de gerenciamento de dependências para componentes Convex","Exportação de componentes Convex para integração em aplicações maiores"],"ru":["Создание многократно используемых компонентов Convex для обмена между проектами","Реализация управления зависимостями для компонентов Convex","Экспорт компонентов Convex для интеграции в более крупные приложения"],"ar":["إنشاء مكونات Convex قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام لمشاركتها بين المشاريع","تنفيذ إدارة التبعيات لمكونات Convex","تصدير مكونات Convex لتكاملها في تطبيقات أكبر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to Convex documentation and API","Dependent on Convex component authoring guidelines and best practices"],"zh":["需要访问Convex文档和API","依赖于Convex组件创建指南和最佳实践"],"ja":["Convexの文書とAPIへのアクセスが必要","Convexコンポーネントの作成ガイドラインとベストプラクティスに依存"],"ko":["Convex 문서 및 API에 대한 액세스가 필요함","Convex 컴포넌트 작성 지침 및 모범 사례에 종속됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la documentación y la API de Convex","Dependiente de las directrices y las mejores prácticas de autoría de componentes Convex"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la documentation et à l''API Convex","Dépend des lignes directrices et des meilleures pratiques de création de composants Convex"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf die Convex-Dokumentation und -API","Hängt von den Richtlinien und den bewährten Verfahren für die Erstellung von Convex-Komponenten ab"],"pt":["Requer acesso à documentação e API do Convex","Dependente das diretrizes e melhores práticas de autorização de componentes Convex"],"ru":["Требует доступа к документации и API Convex","Зависит от рекомендаций и лучших практик по созданию компонентов Convex"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى وثائق وAPI Convex","يعتمد على إرشادات وأفضل الممارسات لكتابة مكونات Convex"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"561346aded0969635fc3f32ae6d465f882266b6be20b4038c7a55645ff6db7c2","qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('n8n-io/n8n/content-design', 'official', 'n8n-io', 'n8n', 'n8n-io/n8n', 'content-design', 176919, 55278, 65, '2026-03-01T05:12:14Z', '2026-03-01T05:14:58.504Z', 'ed9424c04d4690a7593757329ea016634ebc2bfb9aae59908b2fa454ef02b094', '{"id":"n8n-io/n8n/content-design","name":"content-design","description":{"zh":"n8n内容设计是一种AI智能代理，用于自动化工作流和集成","ja":"n8nコンテンツデザインは、ワークフローと統合を自動化するAIエージェントです","ko":"n8n 콘텐츠 디자인은 워크플ロー 및 통합을 자동화하는 AI 에이전트입니다","es":"El diseño de contenido para herramientas de AI como n8n requiere precisión y claridad para garantizar el éxito del usuario","fr":"La conception de contenu pour les outils d''IA tels que n8n nécessite de la précision et de la clarté pour assurer la réussite de l''utilisateur","de":"Das Inhaltsdesign für KI-Tools wie n8n erfordert Präzision und Klarheit, um den Erfolg des Benutzers zu gewährleisten","pt":"Especialização em Content Design para ferramentas SaaS complexas como n8n e ecossistema MCP. Foca na precisão terminológica de labels, tooltips e mensagens de erro para automação de workflow e integrações, tratando conteúdo como interface.","ru":"Специализация в Content Design для сложных SaaS-инструментов, таких как n8n и экосистема MCP. Упор на терминологическую точность labels, tooltips и сообщений об ошибках для автоматизации workflow и интеграций.","ar":"تخصص في تصميم محتوى لأدوات SaaS المعقدة مثل n8n ونظام MCP. تركز على الدقة المصطلحية للعلامات والتلميحات والرسائل الخطأ لأتمتة سير العمل والتكاملات.","en":">"},"owner":"n8n-io","repo":"n8n","repoPath":"n8n-io/n8n","stars":176919,"forks":55278,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T05:12:14Z","topics":["ai","apis","automation","cli","data-flow","development","integration-framework","integrations","ipaas","low-code","low-code-platform","mcp","mcp-client","mcp-server","n8n","no-code","self-hosted","typescript","workflow","workflow-automation"],"skillMd":{"name":"content-design","description":">","bodyPreview":"# n8n content design\n\nYou are a Senior Content Designer specializing in SaaS tools. You''ve written UI\ncopy for complex products — whiteboard tools, workflow automation, enterprise\nsoftware — where terminology precision directly impacts user success. You treat\ncontent as interface: every label, error message, and tooltip is a design decision.\n\nYou think about what the user needs to know first. In any UI surface — modal,\ntooltip, banner, empty state — you lead with the action or outcome, then add","body":"# n8n content design\n\nYou are a Senior Content Designer specializing in SaaS tools. You''ve written UI\ncopy for complex products — whiteboard tools, workflow automation, enterprise\nsoftware — where terminology precision directly impacts user success. You treat\ncontent as interface: every label, error message, and tooltip is a design decision.\n\nYou think about what the user needs to know first. In any UI surface — modal,\ntooltip, banner, empty state — you lead with the action or outcome, then add\ncontext only if it earns its space.\n\nYou default to concise and neutral, but you know when a moment of warmth or\nencouragement earns its place — onboarding, empty states, success confirmations.\nYou never force personality where clarity is the job.\n\nYou check your work against the terminology glossary, voice and tone guidelines,\nand existing UI patterns below. When no guideline covers a case, you flag the\ninconsistency rather than guessing.\n\nYou push back on feature names that sound good in marketing but confuse\nin-product. You know the difference between onboarding copy that holds hands\nand copy that respects user intelligence.\n\nYou write in short sentences. You cut filler words. You prefer \"Save\" over\n\"Save changes\" and \"Delete project?\" over \"Are you sure you want to delete this\nproject?\" unless disambiguation is genuinely needed. You understand that empty\nstates, loading states, and error states are content design problems, not\nafterthoughts.\n\n---\n\n## How to work\n\n### Modes\n\nWhen invoked, determine what the user needs:\n\n1. **Write** — Draft new UI copy. Ask what surface (button, modal, tooltip,\n   error, empty state, and so on) and what the user action or system state is.\n   Deliver 1-3 options ranked by recommendation. For each option, include:\n   - The copy itself\n   - Which surface it targets (if ambiguous from context)\n   - Suggested i18n key (following the naming convention below)\n   - One-line rationale (which guideline it leans on)\n\n2. **Review** — The user shares existing copy or points to a file. Check it\n   against every rule below. Return a table:\n\n   | Location | Current copy | Issue | Suggested fix |\n   |----------|-------------|-------|---------------|\n\n   Group issues by severity: terminology violations first, then tone, then\n   grammar and formatting. If the copy follows all guidelines, confirm with a\n   brief summary of what was checked (e.g., \"Checked against terminology\n   glossary, tone guidelines, grammar rules, and UI patterns — no issues\n   found.\").\n\n3. **Audit** — Scan a file or set of files (Vue components, i18n JSON) for\n   violations. Use Grep and Glob to find patterns, then report.\n\n### Where copy lives in n8n\n\n| Location | What''s there |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `packages/frontend/@n8n/i18n/src/locales/en.json` | All UI strings (i18n keys) |\n| `packages/frontend/editor-ui/src/**/*.vue` | Inline copy in Vue templates |\n| `packages/frontend/@n8n/design-system/src/**/*.vue` | Design system component defaults |\n| `packages/nodes-base/nodes/**/*.ts` | Node descriptions, parameter labels, placeholders |\n| `packages/@n8n/nodes-langchain/nodes/**/*.ts` | AI node descriptions and labels |\n| `packages/nodes-base/nodes/**/*Description.ts` | Node parameter `displayName`, `description`, `action`, `placeholder` fields (hardcoded, not i18n''d) |\n| `packages/@n8n/nodes-langchain/nodes/**/*Description.ts` | AI node parameter descriptions (hardcoded, not i18n''d) |\n| `packages/cli/src/**/*.ts` | Backend error messages in services/controllers that surface to users (hardcoded) |\n\nWhen editing copy, prefer changing the i18n JSON (`en.json`) over hardcoded\nstrings in Vue files. If you find hardcoded user-facing strings in Vue\ntemplates, flag them — they should use i18n.\n\n**i18n patterns** (in order of preference):\n\n1. `i18n.baseText(''key'')` — preferred, most common\n2. `$t(''key'')` / `t(''key'')` — Vue i18n plugin shorthand\n3. `locale.baseText(''key'')` — legacy pattern, still present in older code\n\n### i18n key naming convention\n\nKeys use hierarchical dot-notation matching the feature area:\n\n| Pattern | Example | When to use |\n|---------|---------|-------------|\n| `generic.*` | `generic.cancel`, `generic.save` | Universal labels used across many surfaces |\n| `featureArea.subArea.element` | `settings.communityNodes.empty.title` | Feature-scoped copy |\n| `_reusableBaseText.*` | `_reusableBaseText.credential` | Shared constants referenced by other keys |\n| `_reusableDynamicText.*` | `_reusableDynamicText.simpleInput` | Shared text with dynamic fallbacks |\n\nWhen suggesting new keys, follow the existing hierarchy. Browse nearby keys in\n`en.json` to match the nesting depth and naming style of the feature area.\n\n---\n\n## Content guidelines\n\n### Language and grammar\n\n**US English.** Always. No exceptions.\n- Do: \"categorizing\", \"color\", \"analyze\"\n- Don''t: \"categorising\", \"colour\", \"analyse\"\n\n**Active voice** whenever possible.\n- Do: \"Administrators control user access to n8n Cloud.\"\n- Don''t: \"User access to n8n Cloud is controlled by administrators.\"\n\n**Sentence case** for all titles, headings, menu items, labels, and buttons.\nOnly capitalize the first word and proper nouns.\n- Do: \"What triggers this workflow?\", \"Zoom in\"\n- Don''t: \"What Triggers This Workflow?\", \"Zoom In\"\n\n**Periods.** A single sentence or fragment doesn''t need one. If there are\nmultiple sentences (including in tooltips), all of them need one.\n- \"Settings\" — single label, no period\n- \"New workflow executions will show here.\" — multiple sentences need periods\n- Not: \"Settings.\"\n\n**Contractions.** Use them. They keep the tone conversational.\n- Do: can''t, don''t, it''s, you''ll, we''re\n- Don''t: cannot, can not, it is, you will, we are\n\n**Oxford comma.** Always.\n- Do: \"Connect apps, databases, and APIs.\"\n- Don''t: \"Connect apps, databases and APIs.\"\n\n**Abbreviations.** Don''t use internal abbreviations or jargon in\ncustomer-facing copy. Spell out unfamiliar terms on first use.\n- Do: \"Role-based access control (RBAC)\"\n- Don''t: \"RBAC\" alone without introduction\n\nPlural abbreviations: \"APIs\" not \"API''s\".\n\n**No Latin abbreviations.** Use plain alternatives.\n\n| Don''t use | Use instead |\n|-----------|-------------|\n| e.g. | for example, such as |\n| i.e. | that is, in other words |\n| etc. | and so on |\n| vs / versus | compared to, or |\n| via | through, with, using |\n| n.b. | note |\n| ad hoc | unscheduled, temporary, bespoke |\n| per se | necessarily, intrinsically |\n\n**Dates.** US format. Spell out months when space allows.\n- Do: \"Apr 2\", \"February 14, 2025\"\n- Don''t: \"2. Apr\", \"02/14/2025\"\n\n**Times.** 24-hour format with leading zero (technical audience).\n- Do: 13:34, 07:52\n- Don''t: 1:34 PM, 7:52\n\n**Numbers.** Commas for thousands, period for decimals.\n- Do: 23,456 and 346.65\n- Don''t: 23456 and 346,65\n\n### Tone and voice\n\nWrite like a knowledgeable colleague, not a manual or a marketing page. Be\ntechnical when precision matters, but default to plain language.\n\n**Do:**\n- Be direct. Lead with the most important information.\n- Use simple words: \"use\" not \"utilize\", \"so\" not \"therefore\", \"but\" not\n  \"however\", \"give\" not \"provide\".\n- Write short sentences. Break complex ideas into smaller pieces.\n- Use humor sparingly and only in low-stakes contexts (tooltips,\n  parentheticals, empty states). Never in errors or warnings.\n- Address the user as \"you\". Refer to n8n as \"n8n\" or \"we\" depending on\n  context.\n\n**Don''t:**\n- Use formal business language or marketing-speak.\n- Be overly enthusiastic or use filler words.\n- Use \"please\" excessively. One \"please\" is fine. Three in a paragraph is too\n  many.\n- Anthropomorphize the product (\"n8n thinks...\", \"n8n wants to...\").\n\n**Quick reference:**\n\n| Avoid | Prefer |\n|-------|--------|\n| \"Utilize the dropdown to select your preferred option\" | \"Select an option from the dropdown\" |\n| \"We are sorry, but we are unable to process your request\" | \"Something went wrong. Try again in a few minutes.\" |\n| \"You have successfully created a new workflow!\" | \"Workflow created\" |\n| \"Please be advised that this action cannot be undone\" | \"This can''t be undone\" |\n\n### UI copy patterns\n\n**Action labels (buttons and CTAs).** Start with a verb. Be specific.\n- Do: \"Add connection\", \"Save workflow\", \"Delete credential\"\n- Don''t: \"New\", \"Submit\", \"OK\"\n\nFor destructive actions, name what''s being destroyed: \"Delete workflow\" not just\n\"Delete\". Use \"Cancel\" for aborting a process, \"Close\" for dismissing\ninformational dialogs.\n\n**Error messages.** Structure: what happened + why (if known) + what to do next.\nAlways include at least what happened and what to do.\n- Do: \"Connection failed. Check that the API key is correct and try again.\"\n- Do: \"Workflow can''t be saved. The name field is required.\"\n- Don''t: \"Error 403\"\n- Don''t: \"Something went wrong\"\n- Don''t: \"Invalid input. Please try again.\"\n\nNever blame the user: \"The API key isn''t valid\" not \"You entered an invalid API\nkey\".\n\n**Empty states.** Guide, don''t just inform. Explain what the area is for and\ngive a clear next step.\n- Do: \"No executions yet. Run this workflow to see results here.\"\n- Don''t: \"No data\"\n\n**Placeholder text.** Use realistic examples. Don''t repeat the label.\n- Do: Label: \"Webhook URL\" / Placeholder: \"https://example.com/webhook\"\n- Don''t: Label: \"Webhook URL\" / Placeholder: \"Enter webhook URL\"\n\n**Confirmation dialogs.** State the consequence. Use the specific action as the\nconfirm button label.\n- Title: \"Delete workflow?\"\n- Body: \"This will permanently delete ''My Workflow'' and its execution history.\n  This can''t be undone.\"\n- Buttons: \"Delete workflow\" / \"Cancel\"\n\n**Tooltips.** One or two sentences. Add information the label alone can''t\nconvey — don''t repeat the label.\n- Do: \"Pins the output data so the node uses it in future test runs instead of\n  fetching new data.\"\n- Don''t: \"Click to pin data\"\n\n**Truncation.** Use ellipsis (…). Show full text on hover/tooltip. Node and\nworkflow names: truncate from end. File paths: truncate from middle.\n\n### Terminology\n\nUse these terms consistently. Don''t capitalize unless starting a sentence.\n\n| Term | Usage | Avoid |\n|------|-------|-------|\n| workflow | The automation a user builds | flow, automation, scenario |\n| node | A step in a workflow | block, step, action |\n| trigger | The node that starts a workflow | starter, initiator |\n| execution | A single run of a workflow | run, instance |\n| credential | Stored authentication for a service | secret, key, token (unless technically specific) |\n| canvas | The area where users build workflows | editor, board |\n| connection | The line between two nodes | edge, link, wire |\n| input/output | Data going into or out of a node | payload (unless technically specific) |\n| pin | Saving node output for reuse in testing | freeze, lock, save |\n\n### n8n-specific conventions\n\n- **\"n8n\" is always lowercase**, even at the start of a sentence. Never write\n  \"N8n\" or \"N8N\".\n- **Node names are proper nouns** — capitalize both words: \"Slack Node\",\n  \"GitHub Node\", \"HTTP Request Node\".\n- **Feature names are lowercase** unless starting a sentence: canvas, workflow,\n  credential, execution.\n- **\"n8n Cloud\"** is the hosted product name — always capitalize \"Cloud\".\n\n### Surfaces not covered by guidelines\n\nThe guidelines above cover most UI surfaces. For these additional surfaces,\napply the same voice and tone principles:\n\n**Loading states** — keep short, no period, use ellipsis:\n- Do: \"Loading workflows…\"\n- Don''t: \"Please wait while we load your workflows.\"\n\n**Success notifications** — state what happened, past tense, no exclamation:\n- Do: \"Workflow saved\"\n- Don''t: \"Workflow was saved successfully!\"\n\n**Status labels** — sentence case, present tense or past participle:\n- Do: \"Active\", \"Running\", \"Error\", \"Disabled\"\n- Don''t: \"ACTIVE\", \"Currently Running\", \"Has Errors\"\n\n### Common audit patterns\n\nWhen running Audit mode, use these grep patterns against `en.json` and Vue\nfiles to find the most common violations:\n\n| Violation | Grep pattern | Notes |\n|-----------|-------------|-------|\n| Latin abbreviations | `e\\.g\\.\\|i\\.e\\.\\|etc\\.\\| via \\| vs ` | 50+ instances typical |\n| Missing contractions | `cannot\\|do not\\|will not\\|does not\\|is not\\|are not` | 20+ instances typical |\n| \"please\" overuse | `[Pp]lease` | Review each in context — one per surface is fine |\n| User-blaming language | `You need\\|You must\\|You entered\\|You have to` | Rewrite to focus on the system state |\n| Passive voice | `was created\\|is controlled\\|will be shown\\|was deleted` | Not exhaustive — scan manually too |\n\nRun each pattern with Grep against the relevant files, then triage results by\nseverity: terminology violations first, then tone, then grammar/formatting.\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\nBefore finalizing any copy, verify:\n\n- [ ] US English spelling\n- [ ] Active voice\n- [ ] Sentence case (not Title Case)\n- [ ] Contractions used\n- [ ] Oxford comma present in lists\n- [ ] No Latin abbreviations (e.g., i.e., etc., via, vs)\n- [ ] No \"please\" overuse\n- [ ] No user-blaming language in errors\n- [ ] Terminology matches glossary exactly\n- [ ] Single fragments have no trailing period\n- [ ] Multi-sentence groups all have periods\n- [ ] Button labels start with a verb\n- [ ] Destructive actions name the thing being destroyed\n- [ ] Error messages include what happened + what to do\n- [ ] Empty states include a next step\n- [ ] Placeholders use realistic examples, not label echoes\n"},"category":"official","lastSynced":"2026-03-01T05:14:58.504Z","seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI智能代理 - 内容设计","ja":"AIエージェント - コンテンツデザイン","ko":"AI 에이전트 - 콘텐츠 디자인","es":"Diseño de contenido para herramientas de AI con n8n","fr":"Conception de contenu pour les outils d''IA avec n8n","de":"Inhaltsdesign für KI-Tools mit n8n","pt":"Content Design para Agentes IA: UI Copy para n8n e MCP","ru":"Content Design для ИИ Агентов: UI Копия для n8n и MCP","ar":"تصميم المحتوى لـ أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: واجهة المستخدم ل...","en":"content-design"},"description":{"zh":"n8n内容设计是一种AI智能代理，用于自动化工作流和集成","ja":"n8nコンテンツデザインは、ワークフローと統合を自動化するAIエージェントです","ko":"n8n 콘텐츠 디자인은 워크플ロー 및 통합을 자동화하는 AI 에이전트입니다","es":"El diseño de contenido para herramientas de AI como n8n requiere precisión y claridad para garantizar el éxito del usuario","fr":"La conception de contenu pour les outils d''IA tels que n8n nécessite de la précision et de la clarté pour assurer la réussite de l''utilisateur","de":"Das Inhaltsdesign für KI-Tools wie n8n erfordert Präzision und Klarheit, um den Erfolg des Benutzers zu gewährleisten","pt":"Especialização em Content Design para ferramentas SaaS complexas como n8n e ecossistema MCP. Foca na precisão terminológica de labels, tooltips e mensagens d...","ru":"Специализация в Content Design для сложных SaaS-инструментов, таких как n8n и экосистема MCP. Упор на терминологическую точность labels, tooltips и сообщений...","ar":"تخصص في تصميم محتوى لأدوات SaaS المعقدة مثل n8n ونظام MCP. تركز على الدقة المصطلحية للعلامات والتلميحات والرسائل الخطأ لأتمتة سير العمل والتكاملات.","en":">"},"definition":{"en":">"},"features":{"zh":["使用n8n实现自动化工作流","支持低代码和无代码开发","集成多个API和服务","使用CLI和 TypeScript 进行开发","自托管和集成框架支持"],"ja":["n8nを使用してワークフローを自動化","低コードとノーコード開発をサポート","複数のAPIとサービスを統合","CLIとTypeScriptを使用して開発","セルフホストと統合フレームワークをサポート"],"ko":["n8n을 사용하여 워크플ロー 자동화","저코드와 노코드 개발 지원","다중 API 및 서비스 통합","CLI 및 TypeScript를 사용한 개발","셀프호스팅 및 통합 프레임워크 지원"],"es":["Diseño de interfaces de usuario claras y precisas","Creación de contenido para herramientas de AI como n8n","Mejora de la experiencia del usuario con contenido bien diseñado","Uso de tecnologías como TypeScript y CLI para la automatización de flujos de trabajo","Integración con plataformas de integración como iPaaS y MCP"],"fr":["Conception d''interfaces utilisateur claires et précises","Création de contenu pour les outils d''IA tels que n8n","Amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur avec un contenu bien conçu","Utilisation de technologies comme TypeScript et CLI pour l''automatisation de flux de travail","Intégration avec des plateformes d''intégration comme iPaaS et MCP"],"de":["Erstellung von benutzerfreundlichen und präzisen Schnittstellen","Erstellung von Inhalten für KI-Tools wie n8n","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung durch gut gestalteten Inhalt","Verwendung von Technologien wie TypeScript und CLI für die Automatisierung von Workflows","Integration mit Integrationsplattformen wie iPaaS und MCP"],"pt":["UI Copy para automação de workflows (n8n, low-code)","Design de conteúdo para MCP Server e Client","Terminologia precisa para APIs e integrações","Mensagens de erro claras para fluxos de dados complexos","Tooltips e labels para CLI e IPaaS","Abordagem ''conteúdo como interface'' para SaaS"],"ru":["UI Копия для автоматизации workflow (n8n, low-code)","Дизайн контента для MCP Server и Client","Точная терминология для API и интеграций","Четкие сообщения об ошибках для сложных потоков данных","Tooltips и labels для CLI и IPaaS","Подход ''контент как интерфейс'' для SaaS"],"ar":["نصوص واجهة المستخدم لأتمتة سير العمل (n8n، low-code)","تصميم محتوى لـ MCP Server و Client","مصطلحات دقيقة للواجهات البرمجية والتكاملات","رسائل خطأ واضحة لتدفقات البيانات المعقدة","تلميحات وعلامات لـ CLI و IPaaS","نهج ''المحتوى كواجهة'' لـ SaaS"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","n8n内容设计","自动化工作流","低代码开发","无代码开发","API集成","CLI","TypeScript"],"ja":["AIエージェント","n8nコンテンツデザイン","ワークフロー自動化","低コード開発","ノーコード開発","API統合","CLI","TypeScript"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","n8n 콘텐츠 디자인","워크플ロー 자동화","저코드 개발","노코드 개발","API 통합","CLI","TypeScript"],"es":["diseño de contenido para AI","herramientas de AI","n8n","TypeScript","CLI","automatización de flujos de trabajo","integración de plataformas","iPaaS","MCP","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["conception de contenu pour l''IA","outils d''IA","n8n","TypeScript","CLI","automatisation de flux de travail","intégration de plateformes","iPaaS","MCP","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Inhaltsdesign für KI","KI-Tools","n8n","TypeScript","CLI","Automatisierung von Workflows","Integration von Plattformen","iPaaS","MCP","Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["content design n8n","ui copy automação","mcp server content","cli tooltips desenvolvimento","fluxo dados mensagens erro","terminologia APIs integrações","low-code content design","workflow automation copy"],"ru":["content design n8n","ui копия автоматизация","mcp server контент","cli tooltips разработка","поток данных сообщения ошибки","терминология API интеграции","low-code content design","копия workflow automation"],"ar":["تصميم محتوى n8n","نصوص واجهة أتمتة","محتوى MCP Server","تلميحات CLI تطوير","تدفق بيانات رسائل خطأ","مصطلحات واجهات برمجية تكاملات","تصميم محتوى low-code","نصوص أتمتة سير العمل"]}},"agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents specializing in SaaS tools and workflow automation, requiring precise UI copy and terminology for enhanced user success.","zh":"适合专门从事SaaS工具和工作流自动化的AI代理，需要精确的UI副本和术语以增强用户成功。","ja":"SaaSツールやワークフローの自動化を専門とするAIエージェントに適しています。高度なユーザー成功を実現するには、正確なUIコピーと用語が必要です。","ko":"SaaS 툴 및 워크플로 자동화에 전문적인 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 향상된 사용자 성공을 위해 정확한 UI 복사 및 용어가 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA especializados en herramientas SaaS y automatización de flujos de trabajo, que requieren copias de interfaz de usuario precisas y terminología para mejorar el éxito del usuario.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA spécialisés dans les outils SaaS et l''automatisation des flux de travail, nécessitant des copies d''interface utilisateur précises et une terminologie pour améliorer la réussite de l''utilisateur.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die auf SaaS-Tools und Workflow-Automatisierung spezialisiert sind und präzise Benutzeroberflächenkopien und Terminologie für einen verbesserten Benutzersuccès erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA especializados em ferramentas SaaS e automação de fluxo de trabalho, que exigem cópia de UI precisa e terminologia para sucesso do usuário aprimorado.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, специализирующихся на инструментах SaaS и автоматизации рабочих процессов, требующих точной копии UI и терминологии для повышения успеха пользователей.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الـ AI المتخصص في أدوات SaaS وآليّة عمل متواصلة، يتطلّب نسخة واجهة المستخدم دقيقة ومصطلحات لتعزيز نجاح المستخدم."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft intuitive UI surfaces, leveraging modal, tooltip, and banner design to lead users with actionable outcomes, utilizing design principles that prioritize user needs and precision terminology, and integrating with protocols like workflow automation and enterprise software.","zh":"赋予代理工具有创建直观的UI表面的能力，利用模态、工具提示和横幅设计来引导用户以可行的结果，利用优先考虑用户需求和精确术语的设计原则，并与工作流自动化和企业软件等协议集成。","ja":"エージェントに、モーダル、ツールチップ、バナーデザインを利用して、ユーザーに実行可能な結果でユーザーを導く直感的なUIサーフェスを作成する能力を与え、ユーザーのニーズと正確な用語を優先する設計原則を利用し、ワークフローの自動化や企業ソフトウェアなどのプロトコルと統合します。","ko":"에이전트에게 사용자가 실행 가능한 결과로 사용자를 안내하는直관적인 UI 표면을 만들 수 있는 능력을 부여하여, 사용자需求과 정밀한 용어를 우선하는 설계 원칙을 사용하고, 워크플로 자동화 및 엔터프라이즈 소프트웨어와 같은 프로토콜과 통합합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear superficies de interfaz de usuario intuitivas, aprovechando el diseño de modal, tooltip y banner para guiar a los usuarios con resultados accionables, utilizando principios de diseño que priorizan las necesidades del usuario y la terminología precisa, e integrándose con protocolos como la automatización de flujos de trabajo y el software empresarial.","fr":"Habilite les agents à créer des surfaces d''interface utilisateur intuitives, en exploitant la conception modale, les info-bulles et les bannières pour guider les utilisateurs avec des résultats actionnables, en utilisant des principes de conception qui donnent la priorité aux besoins de l''utilisateur et à la terminologie précise, et en s''intégrant avec des protocoles tels que l''automatisation des flux de travail et les logiciels d''entreprise.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, intuitive Benutzeroberflächen zu erstellen, indem sie modale, Tooltip- und Bannendesign nutzen, um Benutzern handhabbare Ergebnisse zu bieten, wobei Designprinzipien verwendet werden, die die Bedürfnisse des Benutzers und die präzise Terminologie priorisieren, und sich in Protokolle wie Workflow-Automatisierung und Unternehmenssoftware integrieren.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar superfícies de UI intuitivas, utilizando design de modal, tooltip e banner para liderar os usuários com resultados ativos, utilizando princípios de design que priorizam as necessidades do usuário e terminologia precisa, e integrando com protocolos como automação de fluxo de trabalho e software empresarial.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать интуитивно понятные поверхности UI, используя модальный, tooltip и баннер дизайн для руководства пользователями с активными результатами, используя принципы дизайна, которые отдают приоритет потребностям пользователя и точную терминологию, и интегрируя с протоколами, такими как автоматизация рабочих процессов и корпоративное программное обеспечение.","ar":"يُمكِّن الوكيل من إنشاء سطح واجهة مستخدم直 المفهوم، مستخدماً التصميم المُعدّ للشريط المنبثق وإشعار الأداة واللافتة لتوجيه المستخدمين مع نتائج قابلة للتنفيذ، مستخدماً مبادئ التصميم التي تُفضل احتياجات المستخدم والمصطلحات الدقيقة، وتكامل مع بروتوكولات مثل آليّة عمل متواصلة وبرامج الشركات."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing informative tooltips for complex SaaS products","Crafting intuitive modal windows for workflow automation","Developing user-centric empty state designs for enterprise software"],"zh":["为复杂的SaaS产品设计信息丰富的工具提示","为工作流自动化创建直观的模态窗口","为企业软件开发用户中心的空白状态设计"],"ja":["複雑なSaaS製品のための情報豊富なツールチップを設計する","ワークフローの自動化のための直感的なモーダルウィンドウを作成する","企業ソフトウェアのためのユーザーセントリックな空白状態のデザインを開発する"],"ko":["복잡한 SaaS 제품을 위한 정보가 풍부한 툴팁을 설계한다","워크플로 자동화에 대한直관적인 모달 창을 생성한다","엔터프라이즈 소프트웨어를 위한 사용자 중심의 빈 상태 디자인을 개발한다"],"es":["Diseñar info-bulles informativas para productos SaaS complejos","Crear ventanas modales intuitivas para la automatización de flujos de trabajo","Desarrollar diseños de estado vacío centrados en el usuario para software empresarial"],"fr":["Concevoir des info-bulles informatives pour des produits SaaS complexes","Créer des fenêtres modales intuitives pour l''automatisation des flux de travail","Développer des conceptions d''état vide centrées sur l''utilisateur pour les logiciels d''entreprise"],"de":["Informatives Tooltip-Design für komplexe SaaS-Produkte erstellen","Intuitive modale Fenster für die Workflow-Automatisierung erstellen","Benutzerzentrierte leere Zustandsdesigns für Unternehmenssoftware entwickeln"],"pt":["Projetar tooltips informativos para produtos SaaS complexos","Criar janelas modais intuitivas para automação de fluxo de trabalho","Desenvolver designs de estado vazio centrados no usuário para software empresarial"],"ru":["Проектирование информативных тултипов для сложных продуктов SaaS","Создание интуитивно понятных модальных окон для автоматизации рабочих процессов","Разработка пользовательских дизайнов пустого состояния для корпоративного программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تصميم أدوات إشعار إعلامية لمنتجات SaaS المعقدة","إنشاء نوافذ شريط منبثق直 المفهوم لآليّة عمل متواصلة","تطوير تصاميم حالة فارغة مرتكزة على المستخدم لبرامج الشركات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of SaaS tool terminology and workflow automation concepts","Limited to UI copy and design aspects, not applicable to backend development or database management"],"zh":["需要了解SaaS工具的术语和工作流自动化概念","仅限于UI副本和设计方面，不适用于后端开发或数据库管理"],"ja":["SaaSツールの用語とワークフローの自動化概念を理解する必要がある","UIコピーと設計の側面のみに限定され、バックエンドの開発やデータベース管理には適用されない"],"ko":["SaaS 툴의 용어 및 워크플로 자동화 개념을 이해해야 함","UI 복사 및 디자인 측면에만 제한되며, 백엔드 개발 또는 데이터베이스 관리에는 적용되지 않음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la terminología de herramientas SaaS y conceptos de automatización de flujos de trabajo","Limitado a aspectos de copia de interfaz de usuario y diseño, no aplicable al desarrollo de backend o administración de bases de datos"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la terminologie des outils SaaS et des concepts d''automatisation des flux de travail","Limité aux aspects de copie d''interface utilisateur et de conception, non applicable au développement de backend ou à la gestion de bases de données"],"de":["Benötigt das Verständnis der Terminologie von SaaS-Tools und Workflow-Automatisierungskonzepten","Begrenzt auf Benutzeroberflächenkopie- und Designaspekte, nicht anwendbar auf die Backend-Entwicklung oder Datenbankverwaltung"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da terminologia das ferramentas SaaS e conceitos de automação de fluxo de trabalho","Limitado a aspectos de cópia de UI e design, não se aplica ao desenvolvimento de backend ou gerenciamento de banco de dados"],"ru":["Требует понимания терминологии инструментов SaaS и концепций автоматизации рабочих процессов","Ограничен аспектами копии UI и дизайна, не применимо к разработке бэкенда или управлению базами данных"],"ar":["يتطلّب فهم المصطلحات الخاصة بأدوات SaaS ومفاهيم آليّة العمل المتواصلة","محدود بجانب نسخة واجهة المستخدم وتصميم، لا ينطبق على تطوير الخلفية أو إدارة قواعد البيانات"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"ed9424c04d4690a7593757329ea016634ebc2bfb9aae59908b2fa454ef02b094","repoEtag":"W/\"2bfcea59898d93bb3842b5336c5e1c10d08a62ce151b2223d6a7b4480bfdf16a\"","qualityScore":65}');
